{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012a3JQbobaf6oZ9c6rDxD77","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t    world.step(dt);\n81\t  },\n82\t  draw(r) {\n83\t    world.draw(r);\n84\t    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n85\t  }\n86\t};\n87\tgame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n88\t  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n89\t  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\t## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\n93\tlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n94\t48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n95\t  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n96\t  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n97\t  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n98\t  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n99\t  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n100\t  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n101\t  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n102\t  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n103\t  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\n104\tand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n105\t[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\n106\tThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\n107\town side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n108\t\n109\t## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\n110\to: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\n111\thorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\n112\tintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\n113\tlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\n114\tworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\n115\teach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n116\t  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n117\t  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n118\t  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n119\t  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n120\t  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n121\t  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n122\t  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n123\t  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n124\t      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n125\t  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n126\t  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n127\t      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n128\t  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n129\t      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n130\t  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n131\t  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n132\t  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n133\t\n134\t## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\n135\thero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\n136\tsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\n137\tup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\n138\tr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\n139\tthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\n140\tEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\n141\tor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\n142\ta blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\n143\ta.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n144\t  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n145\t  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n146\t  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n147\t  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n148\t  half), e => ...) on actors.\n149\t\n150\t## Props, platforms and things\n151\t  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n152\t  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n153\t  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n154\t  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n155\t  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n156\t  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n157\t  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n158\t  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n159\t  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n160\t  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n161\t  it), data }. Add a kind:\n162\t  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n163\t  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n164\t  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n165\t  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n166\t  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n167\t  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n168\t\n169\t## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n170\t  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n171\t  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n172\t  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n173\t      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n174\t      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n175\t  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n176\t  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n177\t  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n178\t  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n179\t  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n180\t\n181\t## The camera: world.camera\n182\t  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n183\t  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n184\t  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n185\t  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n186\t  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n187\t  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n188\t  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n189\t  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n190\t  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n191\t  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n192\t  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n193\t  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n194\t  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n195\t  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n196\t  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n197\t  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n198\t  when !camera.tank)\n199\t  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n200\t  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n201\t  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n202\t  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n203\t  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n204\t\n205\t## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n206\tterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n207\tcells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\n208\ts1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\n209\tcollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\n210\tand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\n211\tsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n212\t\n213\t## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\n214\tworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\n215\tE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\n216\tRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n217\t{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\n218\tdrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\n219\tbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\n220\tworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\n221\tthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\n222\tshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n223\t'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\n224\tand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n225\t}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\n226\tworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n227\t[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\n228\twindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\n229\tloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\n230\tcharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\n231\tcamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\n232\theight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\n233\tSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\n234\tanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n235\t\n236\t## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\n237\tcamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\n238\tin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\n239\tcleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\n240\tahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n241\t\n242\t## The look\n243\t  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n244\t  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n245\t  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n246\t  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n247\t  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n248\t\n249\t## Your own three.js\n250\tE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\n251\tunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\n252\tMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\n253\tthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\n254\tover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\n255\tnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n256\t\n257\t## Tests\n258\tHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\n259\truns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n260\t*/\n261\timport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"5be77501-293a-4e78-a266-d117e23bb9d1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:43.218Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/skiller7-plan-research-qbSZb9/engine/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js","content":"    world.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    world.draw(r);\n    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n  }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n```\n\n## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\nlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\nand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\nThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\nown side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n\n## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\no: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\nhorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\nintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\nlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\nworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\neach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n\n## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\nhero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\nsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\nup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\nr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\nthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\nEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\nor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\na blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\na.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n  half), e => ...) on actors.\n\n## Props, platforms and things\n  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n  it), data }. Add a kind:\n  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n\n## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n\n## The camera: world.camera\n  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n  when !camera.tank)\n  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n\n## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\nterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\ncells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\ns1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\ncollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\nand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\nsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n\n## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\nworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\nE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\nRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\ndrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\nbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\nworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\nthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\nshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\nand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\nworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\nwindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\nloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\ncharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\ncamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\nheight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\nSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\nanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n\n## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\ncamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\nin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\ncleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\nahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n\n## The look\n  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n\n## Your own three.js\nE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\nunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\nMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\nthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\nover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\nnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n\n## Tests\nHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\nruns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n*/\nimport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';","numLines":182,"startLine":80,"totalLines":3302}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012a3JQbobaf6oZ9c6rDxD77","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
