{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WiFFESN2cT5gAmpMbRz9sf","type":"tool_result","content":"1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n....\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n....\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n....\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false \n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and appli\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"476c54dd-8092-4d66-9e37-0a6a803fa172","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:44.060Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n....\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n....\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n....\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false \n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and appli\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WiFFESN2cT5gAmpMbRz9sf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
