{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2btTSkxF1n2ZYWCJWK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pg8EWwcrMRTcVUrcgt4SLV","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5582,"cache_read_input_tokens":469164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5582},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"a744140c-ae32-46fd-97bb-8c5d57c37e44","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:43.060Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2btCob4NDtdPdPum3V","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Pg8EWwcrMRTcVUrcgt4SLV":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pg8EWwcrMRTcVUrcgt4SLV","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t\n141\t## 5. Architecture\n142\t\n143\t### 5.1 The built page, in order\n144\t\n145\t```html\n146\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n147\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n148\t<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 … pasted unmodified … */</script>       <!-- first script, right after charset -->\n149\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n150\t<title>Skiller7 — Seven Killers, One Mountain</title>\n151\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Seven killers share one body and one mountain. Ride the rails, stop, scan for the laughing invisible Whiteouts and shoot the warm spot.\">\n152\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#d81e2a\">\n153\t<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,…a red 7 on white…\">\n154\t<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Killer7\">\n155\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n156\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">\n157\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n158\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n159\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n160\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n161\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fastest down the Black Run wins; crits cut time\">\n162\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Hold W/✕ ski · S/○ stop · RMB/L2 aim · LMB/R2 shoot · Space/L1 scan\">\n163\t<script type=\"importmap\">{ …§4… }</script>\n164\t<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden} #stage{position:relative;width:100%;height:100%}\n165\t#view{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:0} #screen{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;image-rendering:pixelated;z-index:1;background:transparent}</style>\n166\t</head><body>\n167\t<!-- E.bootSplash('SKILLER7') markup: the splash shows while scripts load -->\n168\t<div id=\"stage\"><canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas></div>\n169\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js v0.85.2 (with S7 PATCHes) */</script>\n170\t<script>/* the Skiller7 bundle: src + content, classic script, defines globalThis.S7, starts nothing */</script>\n171\t<script type=\"module\">/* engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js v0.85.2: imports three and Rapier through the import map */</script>\n172\t<script type=\"module\">S7.start({ World3D: My3D2dge.World3D });</script>\n173\t<script>/* watchdog: if S7.started is still false after 20 s, show \"The 3D libraries didn't load. Check the connection and reload.\" with a Reload button; in a session, call AIHub.fail(that message) */</script>\n174\t</body></html>\n175\t```\n176\tThe build escapes every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n177\t\n178\t### 5.2 Sim and presenter\n179\t\n180\t```\n181\t            game.input ──► Intent layer ◄── Bot (attract, tests)\n182\t                               │ intents (move, turn, branch, aim yaw/pitch deltas, fire, scan, skill, interact…)\n183\t                               ▼\n184\t  ┌──────────────── SIM (deterministic, fixed step 1/120 s, runs in Node) ────────────────┐\n185\t  │ rails · walker · camera director · personas · weapons · skills · whiteouts · combat  │\n186\t  │ scan · bosses · economy · items · gates · story/beats · saves · results · echo run    │\n187\t  └──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘\n188\t                     state (read only)                   events (S7.bus)\n189\t                                 ▼                              ▼\n190\t        Presenter3D (browser) / NullPresenter (Node)      Audio · UI widgets · HUD\n191\t        World3D worlds, actors, rigs, pen, glows,         (headless-safe; audio no-ops\n192\t        lights, FX, first-person overlay, camera          without an AudioContext)\n193\t```\n194\t- **The sim** owns all game state. It uses only the 2D engine (`E.Path`, `E.rng`, `E.Story`, `E.Dialog`, `E.Menu`,\n195\t  `game.input`, `game.audio.pos`, `game.saves`, `game.script`, `game.tween`) and our own math. It never touches three.js,\n196\t  the DOM or `E.World3D`, and it never reads anything back from the presenter.\n197\t- **The presenter** turns state into pictures. It has two hooks: `step(dt)` in the play scene's update after\n198\t  `sim.update` (mirror actors, `rig.update`, `world.step`) and `draw(r)` (pen, glows, lights, `world.draw(r)`, then the\n199\t  HUD). **NullPresenter** has the same interface and does nothing; Node tests use it.\n200\t- **Mouse picking goes through intents.** The UI projects world anchors with `world.project` and turns a hover or a\n201\t  click into an intent (`branch = 2`, `interact = 'murmel'`). The sim also keeps its own simple projection (from the\n202\t  camera director's pose) for stick-to-branch mapping, so headless play needs no presenter.\n203\t- Level geometry exists twice from one source: the presenter builds `World3D` from the area's rows or terrain\n204\t  function, and the sim builds a `LevelGrid` from the same data for line of sight and paths.\n205\t\n206\t### 5.3 Source tree (dev folder)\n207\t\n208\t```\n209\tSkiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174752/\n210\t  package.json            { \"type\": \"module\", devDependencies: { playwright: \"1.63.0\" },\n211\t                            scripts: { build: \"node tools/build.mjs\", test: \"node tests/run.mjs\" } }\n212\t  engine/                 a copy of dist/handoff/ (my-3d2dge.js patched; kits/, tools/, src/assets/…) + my-3d2dge-3d.js (§4)\n213\t  vendor/                 three-0.182.0/, rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/, aihub/               (§4)\n214\t  ref/                    3D starter slices, for reading\n215\t  src/\n216\t    00-core.js        S7 namespace, VERSION, S7.bus, registries (S7.area/persona/weapon/enemy/item/beat/song/voice),\n217\t                      named E.rng streams ('spawn','spread','laugh','fx'), units (M = 16 world units = 1 m)\n218\t    01-math.js        vectors, ray–sphere, ray–capsule, segment distance, angles, easing helpers\n219\t    02-tuning.js      TUNING table {key: {def, min, max, step, label, group}}, live values, reset, difficulty multipliers\n220\t    05-input.js       the S7 input preset, intent layer (human and bot), last-device tracking, idle timer,\n221\t                      touch-only detection, mouse modes (look / pointer), stick flick detection\n222\t    10-levelgrid.js   LevelGrid from level rows and legend (floor and wall heights, pits, stairs, platforms),\n223\t                      terrain sampler, line of sight (tile DDA with heights / terrain ray-march), BFS flow fields\n224\t    11-rails.js       RailGraph (nodes, edges as E.Path), Walker (walk, ski, lift, jump, stairs), junctions,\n225\t                      gate checks, spot proximity\n226\t    12-camera.js      CameraDirector: shots, cuts, blends, aim transition, overrides, shake; sim-side projection\n227\t    20-personas.js    roster state, HP, stats, availability, switching, frozen/fallen\n228\t    21-weapons.js     fire cycles, magazines, reloads, spread, recoil, hitscan/cone/lob kinds, effective range\n229\t    22-skills.js      flare, tuck, longlook, makeitrain + buyout, echo, flash, charge, rescue\n230\t    30-whiteouts.js   enemy types, behaviours, warm spots, tells (footprints, breath), laugh scheduling,\n231\t                      spawner, waves\n232\t    31-combat.js      damage pipeline; hits on enemies, props and targets; crits; explosions; projectiles\n233\t                      (snowballs, suitcases, medals, shells); drops and pickup magnet\n234\t    32-scan.js        scan pulse, reveal timers, laugh-direction cues\n235\t    33-bosses.js      boss controllers: grau, jollyfour, hansi (with phases)\n236\t    40-economy.js     Red, Rime, healing, Wax Bench costs and effects\n237\t    41-items.js       inventory, key items, collectibles, Dossier entries\n238\t    42-gates.js       gate kinds: rope, jump, farbell, buyout, echowall, crystal, exposure, codelock, cornice,\n239\t                      serac, icelock, edelweiss, key\n240\t    50-story.js       E.Story setup, people (speaker ↔ rig ↔ voice), flags, objectives, beats (game.script),\n241\t                      title cards, letterbox\n242\t    51-npcs.js        Murmel hints, Pim appearances, phones, frozen tableaux\n243\t    52-room7.js       entering and leaving, the clock, the Wax Bench, the Wardrobe, the bed, the telephone\n244\t    60-save.js        serialize/deserialize, game.saves wiring, autosave, versions and migrate\n245\t    61-results.js     per-target stats and ranks\n246\t    70-audio.js       buses, song table, SFX definitions, positional helper, music state (layers, cues), ambience\n247\t    71-voice.js       Animalese voice synth and its dialog hookup\n248\t    72-laugh.js       laughter synth (styles) and positional emitters\n249\t    80-ui-kit.js      canvas widget kit: focus lists, buttons, sliders, toggles, tabs, grids, glyph prompts;\n250\t                      pad, keys and mouse (hover focuses, click activates, drag moves sliders)\n251\t    81-hud.js         the in-play HUD\n252\t    82-screens.js     title, Featherbed ring, junction markers, Wax Bench, Wardrobe, map, Dossier and items,\n253\t                      code lock, target cards, results, game over, About/Credits, touch-only notice,\n254\t                      attract overlay\n255\t    83-shell.js       a themed E.Shell (pause, settings, controls, help, saves) and its pause items\n256\t    84-dev.js         dev mode panel and dev overlays\n257\t    85-bot.js         the bot: route runner, rail navigation, combat (used by attract mode and tests)\n258\t    86-attract.js     attract director: vignettes, cheats, any-input exit\n259\t    87-hub.js         AI Hub session flow, Echo Run networking, solo echo recording\n260\t    88-echorun.js     Echo Run rules: course, timing, penalties, results\n261\t    90-present3d.js   Presenter3D: a world per area, actor mirroring, rigs, accessories, pen drawing,\n262\t                      glows, lights, camera\n263\t    91-fx3d.js        snowfall, footprint and red-snow decals, breath, scan ring, splashes, flurry transition\n264\t    92-firstperson.js weapon models and their animations on the overlay pen\n265\t    93-present-null.js NullPresenter\n266\t    95-scenes.js      scenes: title, attract, play (Room 7 is a mode of play), results, credits, gameover,\n267\t                      echorun, hub\n268\t    99-start.js       S7.start(opts): new E.Game, boot steps, scenes, game.debug\n269\t  content/\n270\t    tuning.js personas.js weapons.js enemies.js items.js shapes.js things3d.js songs.js voices.js\n271\t    attract.js echorun.js\n272\t    areas/  room7.js 00A-lobby.js 00B-thirdfloor.js 01A-village.js 01B-palais.js 01C-blackrun.js\n273\t            01D-gondola.js 01E-archive.js 01F-summit.js\n274\t    story/  common.js t00.js t01.js epilogue.js barks.js\n275\t  tools/   build.mjs  validate-content.mjs  fetch-deps.mjs\n276\t  tests/   run.mjs  lib/node-harness.mjs  lib/browser-harness.mjs  node/*.test.mjs  browser/*.test.mjs  out/\n277\t```\n278\t`content/things3d.js` only defines `S7.things3d = W3 => { W3.THINGS.chandelier = (pen, t, time) => …; … }`, and\n279\tPresenter3D calls it in its init, so nothing there runs in Node. Everything else in `content/` is plain data and runs\n280\tanywhere.\n281\t\n282\t### 5.4 The play loop and the mode machine\n283\t\n284\tThe play scene (`pausable: true`, `touch: []`):\n285\t```\n286\tupdate(dt):  if (ui.modal) { ui.modal.update(dt); return; }   // dev panel, Wax Bench, map… freeze the sim\n287\t             intents = Intent.read(game.input | bot)            // one place turns devices into intents\n288\t             sim.update(dt, intents)                            // everything in §7, in a fixed order\n289\t             presenter.step(dt)                                 // mirror, rigs, world.step (browser only)\n290\tdraw(r):     presenter.draw(r)                                  // world.draw, then the HUD and screens\n291\t```\n292\t`sim.update` order: modes → walker → camera director → skills → weapons and projectiles → whiteouts → scan and\n293\treveals → combat resolution → pickups → economy → bosses → triggers and waves → story and beats → results clock →\n294\temit events.\n295\t\n296\t**Modes** (one at a time; `S7.sim.mode`):\n297\t\n298\t| Mode | Enter | Exit | Notes |\n299\t|---|---|---|---|\n300\t| `rail` | default | — | move, turn, interact, heal, skill, ring, aim |\n301\t| `junction` | arrive at a node with 3+ edges | a branch is chosen and move is held | the walker is stopped; branch markers show |\n302\t| `aim` | aim held (or toggled) in rail/lift mode, or on a ski edge after a hockey stop | aim released | first person; the walker is stopped except on lifts and `aimOnTheMove` edges |\n303\t| `ski` | on a `ski` edge | leave the edge | automatic downhill movement; move = tuck, turn = hockey stop |\n304\t| `lift` | board a lift node | the end node | automatic movement; aiming allowed |\n305\t| `talk` | interact with an NPC, phone or tableau | the dialog ends | sim frozen except ambience |\n306\t| `ring` | hold ring | release (switch) | time × 0.15 |\n307\t| `switching` | a persona is chosen | 0.45 s later | invulnerable |\n308\t| `cutscene` | a beat script takes the camera | the script ends | skippable with start/pause → \"Skip scene?\" |\n309\t| `frozen` | the active persona's HP reaches 0 | 1.2 s later → `rescue` | the freeze animation |\n310\t| `rescue` | after `frozen` | the statue is chipped free | you play the Sweep |\n311\t| `gameover` | the Sweep's HP reaches 0 | Continue or Quit | |\n312\t| `modal` | a canvas screen opens | it closes | the sim is frozen |\n313\t\n314\t### 5.5 Data formats (the designer's tools)\n315\t\n316\tAll content is data in `content/`, checked by `tools/validate-content.mjs` (§14.7). **Units in area data:** x and y\n317\tin **tiles** (1 tile = 1 m = 16 world units; row 0 is north, column 0 is west), z in **metres**. The loader multiplies\n318\tby 16. Use `.5` for tile centres.\n319\t\n320\t```js\n321\tS7.area('00A', {\n322\t  title: 'GRAND HOTEL NADA', sub: 'LOBBY', target: 0, music: 'hotel', ambience: 'roomtone',\n323\t  world: {                                   // given to new E.World3D(game, …) and parsed by the sim's LevelGrid\n324\t    level: { rows: [/* 28 strings of 40 chars */], legend: { /* World3D legend: floor, wall, pillar, stairs,\n325\t             platform, pit, torch, mark, shape */ }, ground: 'tiles', colors: { a: '#e8e4dc', b: '#2a2226', size: 2 },\n326\t             side: 'block', color: '#3a2a2e' },\n327\t    // or terrain: { size, height: (x, y) => z /* world units, pure and shared with the sim */, color, rock, far }\n328\t    sky: '#05040a', fog: { color: '#0a0608', near: 40, far: 420 }, ambient: ['#3a2a3a', '#120a0e', 1.2],\n329\t    torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 1, lights: 6, glowLights: 6, overlay: { fov: 62 }, look: 'card', res: 'pixels',\n330\t    filter: { look: 'cel', bands: 3, ink: 1, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.4 },\n331\t    camera: { mode: 'fixed', near: 1 }\n332\t  },\n333\t  nodes: {                                   // t: [x, y, z?]; z defaults to the floor or terrain height there\n334\t    r7: { t: [33.5, 20.5], kind: 'room7' },  j1: { t: [28.5, 20.5], kind: 'junction' },\n335\t    x1: { t: [20.5, 2.5, 6], kind: 'exit', label: 'STAIRS', to: ['00B', 'x1'], needs: { item: 'servicekey' } }\n336\t  },\n337\t  edges: [\n338\t    { id: 'r7-j1', a: 'r7', b: 'j1', kind: 'walk',  // walk | ski | lift | jump | stairs; via: [[x, y, z?], …] bends\n339\t      via: [[31, 20.8]], cams: [{ s: [0, 1], shot: 'fixed', at: [36, 24, 3.2], look: 'hero', fov: 50 }] },"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"314de094-1ec9-4b9d-8a53-535f3afded30","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:43.067Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n## 5. Architecture\n\n### 5.1 The built page, in order\n\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 … pasted unmodified … */</script>       <!-- first script, right after charset -->\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Skiller7 — Seven Killers, One Mountain</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Seven killers share one body and one mountain. Ride the rails, stop, scan for the laughing invisible Whiteouts and shoot the warm spot.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#d81e2a\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,…a red 7 on white…\">\n<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Killer7\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fastest down the Black Run wins; crits cut time\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Hold W/✕ ski · S/○ stop · RMB/L2 aim · LMB/R2 shoot · Space/L1 scan\">\n<script type=\"importmap\">{ …§4… }</script>\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden} #stage{position:relative;width:100%;height:100%}\n#view{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:0} #screen{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;image-rendering:pixelated;z-index:1;background:transparent}</style>\n</head><body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('SKILLER7') markup: the splash shows while scripts load -->\n<div id=\"stage\"><canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas></div>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js v0.85.2 (with S7 PATCHes) */</script>\n<script>/* the Skiller7 bundle: src + content, classic script, defines globalThis.S7, starts nothing */</script>\n<script type=\"module\">/* engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js v0.85.2: imports three and Rapier through the import map */</script>\n<script type=\"module\">S7.start({ World3D: My3D2dge.World3D });</script>\n<script>/* watchdog: if S7.started is still false after 20 s, show \"The 3D libraries didn't load. Check the connection and reload.\" with a Reload button; in a session, call AIHub.fail(that message) */</script>\n</body></html>\n```\nThe build escapes every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n\n### 5.2 Sim and presenter\n\n```\n            game.input ──► Intent layer ◄── Bot (attract, tests)\n                               │ intents (move, turn, branch, aim yaw/pitch deltas, fire, scan, skill, interact…)\n                               ▼\n  ┌──────────────── SIM (deterministic, fixed step 1/120 s, runs in Node) ────────────────┐\n  │ rails · walker · camera director · personas · weapons · skills · whiteouts · combat  │\n  │ scan · bosses · economy · items · gates · story/beats · saves · results · echo run    │\n  └──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘\n                     state (read only)                   events (S7.bus)\n                                 ▼                              ▼\n        Presenter3D (browser) / NullPresenter (Node)      Audio · UI widgets · HUD\n        World3D worlds, actors, rigs, pen, glows,         (headless-safe; audio no-ops\n        lights, FX, first-person overlay, camera          without an AudioContext)\n```\n- **The sim** owns all game state. It uses only the 2D engine (`E.Path`, `E.rng`, `E.Story`, `E.Dialog`, `E.Menu`,\n  `game.input`, `game.audio.pos`, `game.saves`, `game.script`, `game.tween`) and our own math. It never touches three.js,\n  the DOM or `E.World3D`, and it never reads anything back from the presenter.\n- **The presenter** turns state into pictures. It has two hooks: `step(dt)` in the play scene's update after\n  `sim.update` (mirror actors, `rig.update`, `world.step`) and `draw(r)` (pen, glows, lights, `world.draw(r)`, then the\n  HUD). **NullPresenter** has the same interface and does nothing; Node tests use it.\n- **Mouse picking goes through intents.** The UI projects world anchors with `world.project` and turns a hover or a\n  click into an intent (`branch = 2`, `interact = 'murmel'`). The sim also keeps its own simple projection (from the\n  camera director's pose) for stick-to-branch mapping, so headless play needs no presenter.\n- Level geometry exists twice from one source: the presenter builds `World3D` from the area's rows or terrain\n  function, and the sim builds a `LevelGrid` from the same data for line of sight and paths.\n\n### 5.3 Source tree (dev folder)\n\n```\nSkiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174752/\n  package.json            { \"type\": \"module\", devDependencies: { playwright: \"1.63.0\" },\n                            scripts: { build: \"node tools/build.mjs\", test: \"node tests/run.mjs\" } }\n  engine/                 a copy of dist/handoff/ (my-3d2dge.js patched; kits/, tools/, src/assets/…) + my-3d2dge-3d.js (§4)\n  vendor/                 three-0.182.0/, rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/, aihub/               (§4)\n  ref/                    3D starter slices, for reading\n  src/\n    00-core.js        S7 namespace, VERSION, S7.bus, registries (S7.area/persona/weapon/enemy/item/beat/song/voice),\n                      named E.rng streams ('spawn','spread','laugh','fx'), units (M = 16 world units = 1 m)\n    01-math.js        vectors, ray–sphere, ray–capsule, segment distance, angles, easing helpers\n    02-tuning.js      TUNING table {key: {def, min, max, step, label, group}}, live values, reset, difficulty multipliers\n    05-input.js       the S7 input preset, intent layer (human and bot), last-device tracking, idle timer,\n                      touch-only detection, mouse modes (look / pointer), stick flick detection\n    10-levelgrid.js   LevelGrid from level rows and legend (floor and wall heights, pits, stairs, platforms),\n                      terrain sampler, line of sight (tile DDA with heights / terrain ray-march), BFS flow fields\n    11-rails.js       RailGraph (nodes, edges as E.Path), Walker (walk, ski, lift, jump, stairs), junctions,\n                      gate checks, spot proximity\n    12-camera.js      CameraDirector: shots, cuts, blends, aim transition, overrides, shake; sim-side projection\n    20-personas.js    roster state, HP, stats, availability, switching, frozen/fallen\n    21-weapons.js     fire cycles, magazines, reloads, spread, recoil, hitscan/cone/lob kinds, effective range\n    22-skills.js      flare, tuck, longlook, makeitrain + buyout, echo, flash, charge, rescue\n    30-whiteouts.js   enemy types, behaviours, warm spots, tells (footprints, breath), laugh scheduling,\n                      spawner, waves\n    31-combat.js      damage pipeline; hits on enemies, props and targets; crits; explosions; projectiles\n                      (snowballs, suitcases, medals, shells); drops and pickup magnet\n    32-scan.js        scan pulse, reveal timers, laugh-direction cues\n    33-bosses.js      boss controllers: grau, jollyfour, hansi (with phases)\n    40-economy.js     Red, Rime, healing, Wax Bench costs and effects\n    41-items.js       inventory, key items, collectibles, Dossier entries\n    42-gates.js       gate kinds: rope, jump, farbell, buyout, echowall, crystal, exposure, codelock, cornice,\n                      serac, icelock, edelweiss, key\n    50-story.js       E.Story setup, people (speaker ↔ rig ↔ voice), flags, objectives, beats (game.script),\n                      title cards, letterbox\n    51-npcs.js        Murmel hints, Pim appearances, phones, frozen tableaux\n    52-room7.js       entering and leaving, the clock, the Wax Bench, the Wardrobe, the bed, the telephone\n    60-save.js        serialize/deserialize, game.saves wiring, autosave, versions and migrate\n    61-results.js     per-target stats and ranks\n    70-audio.js       buses, song table, SFX definitions, positional helper, music state (layers, cues), ambience\n    71-voice.js       Animalese voice synth and its dialog hookup\n    72-laugh.js       laughter synth (styles) and positional emitters\n    80-ui-kit.js      canvas widget kit: focus lists, buttons, sliders, toggles, tabs, grids, glyph prompts;\n                      pad, keys and mouse (hover focuses, click activates, drag moves sliders)\n    81-hud.js         the in-play HUD\n    82-screens.js     title, Featherbed ring, junction markers, Wax Bench, Wardrobe, map, Dossier and items,\n                      code lock, target cards, results, game over, About/Credits, touch-only notice,\n                      attract overlay\n    83-shell.js       a themed E.Shell (pause, settings, controls, help, saves) and its pause items\n    84-dev.js         dev mode panel and dev overlays\n    85-bot.js         the bot: route runner, rail navigation, combat (used by attract mode and tests)\n    86-attract.js     attract director: vignettes, cheats, any-input exit\n    87-hub.js         AI Hub session flow, Echo Run networking, solo echo recording\n    88-echorun.js     Echo Run rules: course, timing, penalties, results\n    90-present3d.js   Presenter3D: a world per area, actor mirroring, rigs, accessories, pen drawing,\n                      glows, lights, camera\n    91-fx3d.js        snowfall, footprint and red-snow decals, breath, scan ring, splashes, flurry transition\n    92-firstperson.js weapon models and their animations on the overlay pen\n    93-present-null.js NullPresenter\n    95-scenes.js      scenes: title, attract, play (Room 7 is a mode of play), results, credits, gameover,\n                      echorun, hub\n    99-start.js       S7.start(opts): new E.Game, boot steps, scenes, game.debug\n  content/\n    tuning.js personas.js weapons.js enemies.js items.js shapes.js things3d.js songs.js voices.js\n    attract.js echorun.js\n    areas/  room7.js 00A-lobby.js 00B-thirdfloor.js 01A-village.js 01B-palais.js 01C-blackrun.js\n            01D-gondola.js 01E-archive.js 01F-summit.js\n    story/  common.js t00.js t01.js epilogue.js barks.js\n  tools/   build.mjs  validate-content.mjs  fetch-deps.mjs\n  tests/   run.mjs  lib/node-harness.mjs  lib/browser-harness.mjs  node/*.test.mjs  browser/*.test.mjs  out/\n```\n`content/things3d.js` only defines `S7.things3d = W3 => { W3.THINGS.chandelier = (pen, t, time) => …; … }`, and\nPresenter3D calls it in its init, so nothing there runs in Node. Everything else in `content/` is plain data and runs\nanywhere.\n\n### 5.4 The play loop and the mode machine\n\nThe play scene (`pausable: true`, `touch: []`):\n```\nupdate(dt):  if (ui.modal) { ui.modal.update(dt); return; }   // dev panel, Wax Bench, map… freeze the sim\n             intents = Intent.read(game.input | bot)            // one place turns devices into intents\n             sim.update(dt, intents)                            // everything in §7, in a fixed order\n             presenter.step(dt)                                 // mirror, rigs, world.step (browser only)\ndraw(r):     presenter.draw(r)                                  // world.draw, then the HUD and screens\n```\n`sim.update` order: modes → walker → camera director → skills → weapons and projectiles → whiteouts → scan and\nreveals → combat resolution → pickups → economy → bosses → triggers and waves → story and beats → results clock →\nemit events.\n\n**Modes** (one at a time; `S7.sim.mode`):\n\n| Mode | Enter | Exit | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `rail` | default | — | move, turn, interact, heal, skill, ring, aim |\n| `junction` | arrive at a node with 3+ edges | a branch is chosen and move is held | the walker is stopped; branch markers show |\n| `aim` | aim held (or toggled) in rail/lift mode, or on a ski edge after a hockey stop | aim released | first person; the walker is stopped except on lifts and `aimOnTheMove` edges |\n| `ski` | on a `ski` edge | leave the edge | automatic downhill movement; move = tuck, turn = hockey stop |\n| `lift` | board a lift node | the end node | automatic movement; aiming allowed |\n| `talk` | interact with an NPC, phone or tableau | the dialog ends | sim frozen except ambience |\n| `ring` | hold ring | release (switch) | time × 0.15 |\n| `switching` | a persona is chosen | 0.45 s later | invulnerable |\n| `cutscene` | a beat script takes the camera | the script ends | skippable with start/pause → \"Skip scene?\" |\n| `frozen` | the active persona's HP reaches 0 | 1.2 s later → `rescue` | the freeze animation |\n| `rescue` | after `frozen` | the statue is chipped free | you play the Sweep |\n| `gameover` | the Sweep's HP reaches 0 | Continue or Quit | |\n| `modal` | a canvas screen opens | it closes | the sim is frozen |\n\n### 5.5 Data formats (the designer's tools)\n\nAll content is data in `content/`, checked by `tools/validate-content.mjs` (§14.7). **Units in area data:** x and y\nin **tiles** (1 tile = 1 m = 16 world units; row 0 is north, column 0 is west), z in **metres**. The loader multiplies\nby 16. Use `.5` for tile centres.\n\n```js\nS7.area('00A', {\n  title: 'GRAND HOTEL NADA', sub: 'LOBBY', target: 0, music: 'hotel', ambience: 'roomtone',\n  world: {                                   // given to new E.World3D(game, …) and parsed by the sim's LevelGrid\n    level: { rows: [/* 28 strings of 40 chars */], legend: { /* World3D legend: floor, wall, pillar, stairs,\n             platform, pit, torch, mark, shape */ }, ground: 'tiles', colors: { a: '#e8e4dc', b: '#2a2226', size: 2 },\n             side: 'block', color: '#3a2a2e' },\n    // or terrain: { size, height: (x, y) => z /* world units, pure and shared with the sim */, color, rock, far }\n    sky: '#05040a', fog: { color: '#0a0608', near: 40, far: 420 }, ambient: ['#3a2a3a', '#120a0e', 1.2],\n    torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 1, lights: 6, glowLights: 6, overlay: { fov: 62 }, look: 'card', res: 'pixels',\n    filter: { look: 'cel', bands: 3, ink: 1, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.4 },\n    camera: { mode: 'fixed', near: 1 }\n  },\n  nodes: {                                   // t: [x, y, z?]; z defaults to the floor or terrain height there\n    r7: { t: [33.5, 20.5], kind: 'room7' },  j1: { t: [28.5, 20.5], kind: 'junction' },\n    x1: { t: [20.5, 2.5, 6], kind: 'exit', label: 'STAIRS', to: ['00B', 'x1'], needs: { item: 'servicekey' } }\n  },\n  edges: [\n    { id: 'r7-j1', a: 'r7', b: 'j1', kind: 'walk',  // walk | ski | lift | jump | stairs; via: [[x, y, z?], …] bends\n      via: [[31, 20.8]], cams: [{ s: [0, 1], shot: 'fixed', at: [36, 24, 3.2], look: 'hero', fov: 50 }] },","numLines":200,"startLine":140,"totalLines":2112}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pg8EWwcrMRTcVUrcgt4SLV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
