{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2egdNvKKjX5YjMASD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KyrsbCmtGTp8VqvPPktN5e","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":499,"limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5906,"cache_read_input_tokens":486177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5906},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"0f998343-d9d9-4162-bc08-2602bc299d11","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:24.443Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2egNW9rS3TDFtyDEpb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KyrsbCmtGTp8VqvPPktN5e":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":499,"limit":150}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KyrsbCmtGTp8VqvPPktN5e","type":"tool_result","content":"499\t\n500\t- **Touch-only** means `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` and no `(any-pointer: fine)` and `navigator.maxTouchPoints >\n501\t  0`, and no gamepad connected, and no key pressed yet.\n502\t- Then the title shows, centred: **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED**, a line \"Connect a controller or a keyboard to\n503\t  play\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap calls `game.menu('settings')`). The corner's menu and full-screen buttons\n504\t  stay. There are **no touch controls**: every scene has `touch: []` and `game.input.touchEnabled = false`.\n505\t- The idle timer still runs: after 10 s the **attract mode** plays (§7.23). A tap stops it and returns to the notice.\n506\t- If a gamepad connects or a key is pressed, the notice is replaced by the normal title at once.\n507\t- In an AI Hub session on a touch-only device, call `AIHub.fail('Controller or keyboard required')`.\n508\t\n509\t---\n510\t\n511\t## 7. Systems\n512\t\n513\tEach system lists its rules, its numbers (**Piste** difficulty unless stated) and its tests. Speeds are world units\n514\tper second (16 = 1 m).\n515\t\n516\t### 7.1 Rails and movement (`11-rails.js`)\n517\t\n518\t**Graph.** Nodes `{ id, at, kind: junction | room7 | exit | door | stop | lift | npc }` and edges\n519\t`{ id, a, b, kind, path (E.Path, catmull), oneWay, gate, cams, tags }`. A walk edge is two-way. Ski, lift and jump\n520\tedges are one-way, a → b. Points without z take the floor height (LevelGrid) or the terrain height there.\n521\t\n522\t**Walker state:** `{ edge, s (distance from a), dir (±1), v, mode }`. Each step: `s += dir·v·dt`; the position is\n523\t`path.at(s)`. Facing is the path's tangent times dir.\n524\t\n525\t| Rule | Value |\n526\t|---|---|\n527\t| Walk speed | 85 × persona factor × (1 + 0.08 × Speed level). Factors: Dagny 1.15, Rurik 0.9, Ignaz 0.9, the rest 1.0 |\n528\t| Accelerate / stop | to full speed in 0.18 s; to a stop in 0.12 s |\n529\t| Quick turn | `dir *= -1` over 0.22 s (the facing turns through 180°); only on two-way edges |\n530\t| Pass-through | a node with 2 edges is passed without stopping |\n531\t| Junction | a node with 3+ edges: decelerate over the last 1.2 m and stop exactly on it, mode `junction` |\n532\t| Dead end | a node with 1 edge: stop |\n533\t| Doors and exits | stop with a prompt \"△ ENTER\"; stair exits (`open: true`) trigger on arrival |\n534\t| Stairs | walk edges with slope: speed × 0.85 |\n535\t| Ski (downhill) | `v += (g·slope − k·v² − μ)·dt`, with g = 520, slope = −dz/ds along the path, k = 0.0011 (tuck 0.0006, carve 0.0019), μ = 6. Top speed 190 (Dagny tucking: 260). A hockey stop decelerates at 600 and holds you at 0 until move |\n536\t| Ski forks | markers appear 2.5 s before the fork; you pick while moving (stick, d-pad, A/D, a click); the default is the branch closest to straight ahead |\n537\t| Lift | board with △ at a lift node: a fixed speed (T-bar 120, gondola 140); aim and switch are allowed; you can't get off mid-way |\n538\t| Jump | only Dagny, and she must be tucking (skill held) or arrive at speed ≥ 150. A ballistic arc over the edge (apex 2.5 m), landing on b. Anyone else stops at the lip: \"TOO FAR TO JUMP.\" |\n539\t\n540\t**Junction choice.** Each branch's first 1.5 m tangent is projected through the director's camera pose to a screen\n541\tangle. The stick picks the branch nearest its angle. D-pad, arrows and A/D cycle. The mouse hover sets it (§6.3). The\n542\thighlighted branch starts as the one nearest straight ahead. Holding move (or a click on a marker) takes it. A gated\n543\tbranch shows the gate's icon and the solver's face. Trying it with the wrong persona plays the gate's line and stays\n544\t(§7.13).\n545\t\n546\t**Tests:** the graph builds from every area and every edge's path length is > 0; walking holds speed and stops on\n547\trelease; quick turn flips dir and only on two-way edges; arrival at a junction stops within 0.1 m; the stick picks\n548\tthe right branch for each of 8 directions under a known camera pose; a ski edge accelerates on a slope and the hockey\n549\tstop brings v to 0; a jump edge refuses everyone but Dagny and lands her on b; lifts carry you end to end in\n550\tlength / speed seconds.\n551\t\n552\t### 7.2 Camera director (`12-camera.js`)\n553\t\n554\t- Picks the shot that covers the walker's `s` on its edge (`cams`, or `rcams` when dir = −1) and computes the pose\n555\t  `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (yaw from +x toward +y, pitch negative looking down, as `world.camera.fixed`\n556\t  takes it).\n557\t- Cuts are hard unless a shot asks for `blend`. A cut also happens on area changes, quick turns (when the shot sets\n558\t  `rev: true`) and beat overrides.\n559\t- **Aim transition:** blend from the current shot to the eye (feet + 1.6 m) over 0.15 s. Leaving takes 0.15 s back.\n560\t- **Follow** shots never sink under the floor or terrain: they are clamped to ground + 1.2 m.\n561\t- **Overrides:** a beat pushes a shot for its length (`G.cam(…)`); boss intros use `orbit`\n562\t  (`center, radius, height, speed`).\n563\t- **Shake** comes from the engine (`game.shake`, which respects the comfort settings).\n564\t- The presenter applies the pose each frame to `world.camera.fixed` (mode `'fixed'`), placed part way between the last\n565\t  two steps by `game.alpha`.\n566\t- The sim keeps `project(x, y, z)` (yaw, pitch, fov, aspect) for junction mapping and bot aiming.\n567\t\n568\t**Tests:** for every edge in every area, shots cover [0, 1] (the validator); a fixed shot looks at the hero (the\n569\thero's projected point is within 10% of the screen centre, vertically 30–70%); the follow clamp holds on a terrain\n570\tedge; the aim transition reaches the eye in 0.15 s ± 1 step.\n571\t\n572\t### 7.3 Aim mode (first person)\n573\t\n574\t- Entering stops the walker (except on lifts and `aimOnTheMove` edges), hides the hero's actor, turns on\n575\t  `world.overlay` with the persona's weapon model (§9), and shows the reticle and ammo. Yaw is free (360°); pitch is\n576\t  clamped to ±70°. You start looking along the rail's facing.\n577\t- **Controller:** max yaw rate 160°/s, pitch 110°/s, response curve `|x|^1.8`, the engine's radial dead zone (.18).\n578\t  After 0.35 s past 90% deflection, the rate ramps up 60% over 0.3 s. Invert Y comes from the engine setting\n579\t  (`invertAimY`).\n580\t- **Aim assist** (controller only; setting Off / Low / High; default Low, High on Bunny Hill): within 3.5° of a\n581\t  revealed warm spot or a gate target, turning slows to 55% (Low) or 40% (High); within 5°, magnetism pulls 12%/s\n582\t  (Low) or 25%/s (High) toward it.\n583\t- **Mouse, look mode** (default): `world.camera.capture = true`, and each step `world.camera.takeMouse()` gives the\n584\t  deltas, at 0.12°/px (the sensitivity slider runs 0.03–0.4). The reticle sits at the centre. If pointer lock fails\n585\t  (an iframe without permission, `pointerlockerror`), switch to pointer mode and toast \"Mouse: pointer mode\".\n586\t- **Mouse, pointer mode** (setting; like a light gun): `world.camera.mouseLook = false`. The reticle follows\n587\t  `input.pointer()`. In the outer 10% of the screen the view pans, up to 120°/s at the edge. The ray goes through the\n588\t  reticle's screen point.\n589\t- **Sway:** a Lissajous wobble of amplitude 0.7° × (1 − 0.15 × Steady), at least 0.1°, at 0.6 / 0.9 Hz. Telemark's\n590\t  scope halves it.\n591\t- **Recoil** kicks pitch up by the weapon's `recoil` and recovers at 10°/s.\n592\t- **The bot** drives aim with the same intents (yaw and pitch rates), limited to human rates with a 0.25 s reaction\n593\t  time (§14.3).\n594\t\n595\t**Tests:** entering and leaving aim holds the walker still; rates and clamps hold; with assist High a still target is\n596\tacquired faster than with Off (bot timing); pointer mode maps a screen point to the right world ray (sim projection).\n597\t\n598\t### 7.4 Weapons and shooting (`21-weapons.js`, `31-combat.js`)\n599\t\n600\tInfinite reserve ammunition: every weapon has a magazine and a reload (Killer7's rule). Reloading starts by itself\n601\twhen you fire an empty gun. **Hitscan:** a ray from the eye along the reticle's direction, plus seeded spread (the\n602\t'spread' rng). It is tested against, nearest first: enemy warm spots (spheres), enemy bodies (capsules), shields,\n603\tshootable props and gate targets (spheres or boxes), projectiles (snowballs, suitcases, medals), and the LevelGrid's\n604\tline of sight (walls, floors, terrain, `blocks`). **Effective range:** beyond `range`, damage falls to 25%. **Far\n605\ttargets** (bells, insulators: gate targets marked `far`) register only a **scoped Gamsbock shot** (Long Look on);\n606\tany other hit on one splashes \"TOO FAR.\" at the hit point, so they stay Ignaz's puzzle whatever the other guns' range.\n607\t\n608\t| Persona | Weapon (`view` model) | Kind | Damage | Interval | Mag | Reload | Spread | Range | Special |\n609\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n610\t| Ansel | **Patrol .38** revolver | hitscan | 24 | 0.40 s | 6 | 1.8 s | 0.4° | 60 m | sets the target burning: 5/s for 3 s |\n611\t| Dagny | **Pole Guns** (two ski poles with barrels; fire alternates) | hitscan, auto | 6 | 0.07 s | 50 | 1.5 s | 2.0° | 35 m | hold to fire |\n612\t| Ignaz | **Gamsbock** hunting rifle | hitscan | 90 | 1.20 s | 5 | 2.4 s | 0° | 120 m (250 scoped) | pierces 1 |\n613\t| Rurik | **Bullion** gold pump shotgun | 10 pellets | 9 each | 0.95 s | 6 | 0.45 s a shell | 8° cone | 25 m | knockback; spins a Plow |\n614\t| Kasimir | **Alphorn** (a sonic blast) | cone 25°, 18 m | 40 to all | 1.00 s | heat: 5 blasts | overheats 2.5 s | — | 18 m | strong knockback; spins a Plow; shatters snowballs |\n615\t| Mireille | **Lady .25** pocket pistol | hitscan | 15 | 0.20 s | 9 | 1.1 s | 0.3° | 70 m | warm spot radius +25% |\n616\t| Brigid | **Avalauncher** (a pneumatic shell launcher) | lob: 300 u/s, gravity 300 | 70 splash, 2.5 m | 1.10 s | 4 | 2.8 s | — | 90 m | explodes on contact or after 2 s; staggers a Plow |\n617\t\n618\t**Recoil (°):** .38 1.2 · Pole Guns 0.3 · Gamsbock 3 · Bullion 4 · Alphorn 2 · Lady .25 0.6 · Avalauncher 3.5.\n619\t**Power** scales damage by +12% a level. **Speed** cuts reload time by 8% a level.\n620\t\n621\t**Tests:** each weapon's fire interval, magazine and reload times match the table to ±1 step; hitscan picks the\n622\tnearest of overlapping volumes; a warm-spot hit is a crit (§7.7); a wall between the eye and the target blocks it; past\n623\trange, damage is 25%; a far target ignores every hit except a scoped Gamsbock shot; the shotgun fires 10 pellets inside its cone; the Alphorn hits\n624\teverything in its cone; Avalauncher shells follow the arc and splash.\n625\t\n626\t### 7.5 Scan, invisibility, tells and laughter (`32-scan.js`, `72-laugh.js`)\n627\t\n628\t- Whiteouts are **invisible** until revealed (`actor.visible = false`). They are still in the world: shots hit them,\n629\t  and a hit reveals one for 3 s.\n630\t- **Tells while invisible:** fresh **footprints** (outdoors in snow they last 8 s; indoors wet prints last 2.5 s), a\n631\t  **breath puff** from head height every 1.2 s, and **laughter**. Laughs are positional, louder and quicker as they\n632\t  near. In the HUD, a **laugh ripple** (a red arc at the screen's edge pointing at the source, its thickness the\n633\t  loudness) shows the 4 loudest; it can be turned off in Settings.\n634\t- **Scan** (aim mode): a ring expands from you to 40 m in 0.6 s. Every Whiteout it touches is revealed for 6 s\n635\t  (+0.4 s a Steady level). Cooldown 1.2 s. When revealed and within 30 m, the warm spot shows: an orange-red glow\n636\t  (`world.glow`) plus a pulsing diamond ring in the HUD.\n637\t- Revealing fades the figure in over 0.25 s with a static flicker. Unrevealing fades it out over 0.4 s.\n638\t- Skills that reveal too: Ansel's Flare (all within 30 m for 8 s), Kasimir's Echo (marks through walls for 5 s), and\n639\t  Mireille's Flash (reveals what is in its cone).\n640\t\n641\t**Tests:** an unrevealed enemy has `visible = false` and still takes hits; a scan reveals exactly the enemies within\n642\tthe ring's radius at the time it passes them; the reveal runs out after 6 s + Steady; footprints are emitted along the\n643\tpath at stride length; the laugh rate rises as distance falls.\n644\t\n645\t### 7.6 Whiteouts: behaviour, spawns, waves (`30-whiteouts.js`)\n646\t\n647\t| Type | HP | Speed | Contact | Red (body / crit) | Rime (crit) | Behaviour |\n648\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"be73f434-2066-4065-bc72-aece8a808e03","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:24.449Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n- **Touch-only** means `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` and no `(any-pointer: fine)` and `navigator.maxTouchPoints >\n  0`, and no gamepad connected, and no key pressed yet.\n- Then the title shows, centred: **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED**, a line \"Connect a controller or a keyboard to\n  play\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap calls `game.menu('settings')`). The corner's menu and full-screen buttons\n  stay. There are **no touch controls**: every scene has `touch: []` and `game.input.touchEnabled = false`.\n- The idle timer still runs: after 10 s the **attract mode** plays (§7.23). A tap stops it and returns to the notice.\n- If a gamepad connects or a key is pressed, the notice is replaced by the normal title at once.\n- In an AI Hub session on a touch-only device, call `AIHub.fail('Controller or keyboard required')`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Systems\n\nEach system lists its rules, its numbers (**Piste** difficulty unless stated) and its tests. Speeds are world units\nper second (16 = 1 m).\n\n### 7.1 Rails and movement (`11-rails.js`)\n\n**Graph.** Nodes `{ id, at, kind: junction | room7 | exit | door | stop | lift | npc }` and edges\n`{ id, a, b, kind, path (E.Path, catmull), oneWay, gate, cams, tags }`. A walk edge is two-way. Ski, lift and jump\nedges are one-way, a → b. Points without z take the floor height (LevelGrid) or the terrain height there.\n\n**Walker state:** `{ edge, s (distance from a), dir (±1), v, mode }`. Each step: `s += dir·v·dt`; the position is\n`path.at(s)`. Facing is the path's tangent times dir.\n\n| Rule | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Walk speed | 85 × persona factor × (1 + 0.08 × Speed level). Factors: Dagny 1.15, Rurik 0.9, Ignaz 0.9, the rest 1.0 |\n| Accelerate / stop | to full speed in 0.18 s; to a stop in 0.12 s |\n| Quick turn | `dir *= -1` over 0.22 s (the facing turns through 180°); only on two-way edges |\n| Pass-through | a node with 2 edges is passed without stopping |\n| Junction | a node with 3+ edges: decelerate over the last 1.2 m and stop exactly on it, mode `junction` |\n| Dead end | a node with 1 edge: stop |\n| Doors and exits | stop with a prompt \"△ ENTER\"; stair exits (`open: true`) trigger on arrival |\n| Stairs | walk edges with slope: speed × 0.85 |\n| Ski (downhill) | `v += (g·slope − k·v² − μ)·dt`, with g = 520, slope = −dz/ds along the path, k = 0.0011 (tuck 0.0006, carve 0.0019), μ = 6. Top speed 190 (Dagny tucking: 260). A hockey stop decelerates at 600 and holds you at 0 until move |\n| Ski forks | markers appear 2.5 s before the fork; you pick while moving (stick, d-pad, A/D, a click); the default is the branch closest to straight ahead |\n| Lift | board with △ at a lift node: a fixed speed (T-bar 120, gondola 140); aim and switch are allowed; you can't get off mid-way |\n| Jump | only Dagny, and she must be tucking (skill held) or arrive at speed ≥ 150. A ballistic arc over the edge (apex 2.5 m), landing on b. Anyone else stops at the lip: \"TOO FAR TO JUMP.\" |\n\n**Junction choice.** Each branch's first 1.5 m tangent is projected through the director's camera pose to a screen\nangle. The stick picks the branch nearest its angle. D-pad, arrows and A/D cycle. The mouse hover sets it (§6.3). The\nhighlighted branch starts as the one nearest straight ahead. Holding move (or a click on a marker) takes it. A gated\nbranch shows the gate's icon and the solver's face. Trying it with the wrong persona plays the gate's line and stays\n(§7.13).\n\n**Tests:** the graph builds from every area and every edge's path length is > 0; walking holds speed and stops on\nrelease; quick turn flips dir and only on two-way edges; arrival at a junction stops within 0.1 m; the stick picks\nthe right branch for each of 8 directions under a known camera pose; a ski edge accelerates on a slope and the hockey\nstop brings v to 0; a jump edge refuses everyone but Dagny and lands her on b; lifts carry you end to end in\nlength / speed seconds.\n\n### 7.2 Camera director (`12-camera.js`)\n\n- Picks the shot that covers the walker's `s` on its edge (`cams`, or `rcams` when dir = −1) and computes the pose\n  `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (yaw from +x toward +y, pitch negative looking down, as `world.camera.fixed`\n  takes it).\n- Cuts are hard unless a shot asks for `blend`. A cut also happens on area changes, quick turns (when the shot sets\n  `rev: true`) and beat overrides.\n- **Aim transition:** blend from the current shot to the eye (feet + 1.6 m) over 0.15 s. Leaving takes 0.15 s back.\n- **Follow** shots never sink under the floor or terrain: they are clamped to ground + 1.2 m.\n- **Overrides:** a beat pushes a shot for its length (`G.cam(…)`); boss intros use `orbit`\n  (`center, radius, height, speed`).\n- **Shake** comes from the engine (`game.shake`, which respects the comfort settings).\n- The presenter applies the pose each frame to `world.camera.fixed` (mode `'fixed'`), placed part way between the last\n  two steps by `game.alpha`.\n- The sim keeps `project(x, y, z)` (yaw, pitch, fov, aspect) for junction mapping and bot aiming.\n\n**Tests:** for every edge in every area, shots cover [0, 1] (the validator); a fixed shot looks at the hero (the\nhero's projected point is within 10% of the screen centre, vertically 30–70%); the follow clamp holds on a terrain\nedge; the aim transition reaches the eye in 0.15 s ± 1 step.\n\n### 7.3 Aim mode (first person)\n\n- Entering stops the walker (except on lifts and `aimOnTheMove` edges), hides the hero's actor, turns on\n  `world.overlay` with the persona's weapon model (§9), and shows the reticle and ammo. Yaw is free (360°); pitch is\n  clamped to ±70°. You start looking along the rail's facing.\n- **Controller:** max yaw rate 160°/s, pitch 110°/s, response curve `|x|^1.8`, the engine's radial dead zone (.18).\n  After 0.35 s past 90% deflection, the rate ramps up 60% over 0.3 s. Invert Y comes from the engine setting\n  (`invertAimY`).\n- **Aim assist** (controller only; setting Off / Low / High; default Low, High on Bunny Hill): within 3.5° of a\n  revealed warm spot or a gate target, turning slows to 55% (Low) or 40% (High); within 5°, magnetism pulls 12%/s\n  (Low) or 25%/s (High) toward it.\n- **Mouse, look mode** (default): `world.camera.capture = true`, and each step `world.camera.takeMouse()` gives the\n  deltas, at 0.12°/px (the sensitivity slider runs 0.03–0.4). The reticle sits at the centre. If pointer lock fails\n  (an iframe without permission, `pointerlockerror`), switch to pointer mode and toast \"Mouse: pointer mode\".\n- **Mouse, pointer mode** (setting; like a light gun): `world.camera.mouseLook = false`. The reticle follows\n  `input.pointer()`. In the outer 10% of the screen the view pans, up to 120°/s at the edge. The ray goes through the\n  reticle's screen point.\n- **Sway:** a Lissajous wobble of amplitude 0.7° × (1 − 0.15 × Steady), at least 0.1°, at 0.6 / 0.9 Hz. Telemark's\n  scope halves it.\n- **Recoil** kicks pitch up by the weapon's `recoil` and recovers at 10°/s.\n- **The bot** drives aim with the same intents (yaw and pitch rates), limited to human rates with a 0.25 s reaction\n  time (§14.3).\n\n**Tests:** entering and leaving aim holds the walker still; rates and clamps hold; with assist High a still target is\nacquired faster than with Off (bot timing); pointer mode maps a screen point to the right world ray (sim projection).\n\n### 7.4 Weapons and shooting (`21-weapons.js`, `31-combat.js`)\n\nInfinite reserve ammunition: every weapon has a magazine and a reload (Killer7's rule). Reloading starts by itself\nwhen you fire an empty gun. **Hitscan:** a ray from the eye along the reticle's direction, plus seeded spread (the\n'spread' rng). It is tested against, nearest first: enemy warm spots (spheres), enemy bodies (capsules), shields,\nshootable props and gate targets (spheres or boxes), projectiles (snowballs, suitcases, medals), and the LevelGrid's\nline of sight (walls, floors, terrain, `blocks`). **Effective range:** beyond `range`, damage falls to 25%. **Far\ntargets** (bells, insulators: gate targets marked `far`) register only a **scoped Gamsbock shot** (Long Look on);\nany other hit on one splashes \"TOO FAR.\" at the hit point, so they stay Ignaz's puzzle whatever the other guns' range.\n\n| Persona | Weapon (`view` model) | Kind | Damage | Interval | Mag | Reload | Spread | Range | Special |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ansel | **Patrol .38** revolver | hitscan | 24 | 0.40 s | 6 | 1.8 s | 0.4° | 60 m | sets the target burning: 5/s for 3 s |\n| Dagny | **Pole Guns** (two ski poles with barrels; fire alternates) | hitscan, auto | 6 | 0.07 s | 50 | 1.5 s | 2.0° | 35 m | hold to fire |\n| Ignaz | **Gamsbock** hunting rifle | hitscan | 90 | 1.20 s | 5 | 2.4 s | 0° | 120 m (250 scoped) | pierces 1 |\n| Rurik | **Bullion** gold pump shotgun | 10 pellets | 9 each | 0.95 s | 6 | 0.45 s a shell | 8° cone | 25 m | knockback; spins a Plow |\n| Kasimir | **Alphorn** (a sonic blast) | cone 25°, 18 m | 40 to all | 1.00 s | heat: 5 blasts | overheats 2.5 s | — | 18 m | strong knockback; spins a Plow; shatters snowballs |\n| Mireille | **Lady .25** pocket pistol | hitscan | 15 | 0.20 s | 9 | 1.1 s | 0.3° | 70 m | warm spot radius +25% |\n| Brigid | **Avalauncher** (a pneumatic shell launcher) | lob: 300 u/s, gravity 300 | 70 splash, 2.5 m | 1.10 s | 4 | 2.8 s | — | 90 m | explodes on contact or after 2 s; staggers a Plow |\n\n**Recoil (°):** .38 1.2 · Pole Guns 0.3 · Gamsbock 3 · Bullion 4 · Alphorn 2 · Lady .25 0.6 · Avalauncher 3.5.\n**Power** scales damage by +12% a level. **Speed** cuts reload time by 8% a level.\n\n**Tests:** each weapon's fire interval, magazine and reload times match the table to ±1 step; hitscan picks the\nnearest of overlapping volumes; a warm-spot hit is a crit (§7.7); a wall between the eye and the target blocks it; past\nrange, damage is 25%; a far target ignores every hit except a scoped Gamsbock shot; the shotgun fires 10 pellets inside its cone; the Alphorn hits\neverything in its cone; Avalauncher shells follow the arc and splash.\n\n### 7.5 Scan, invisibility, tells and laughter (`32-scan.js`, `72-laugh.js`)\n\n- Whiteouts are **invisible** until revealed (`actor.visible = false`). They are still in the world: shots hit them,\n  and a hit reveals one for 3 s.\n- **Tells while invisible:** fresh **footprints** (outdoors in snow they last 8 s; indoors wet prints last 2.5 s), a\n  **breath puff** from head height every 1.2 s, and **laughter**. Laughs are positional, louder and quicker as they\n  near. In the HUD, a **laugh ripple** (a red arc at the screen's edge pointing at the source, its thickness the\n  loudness) shows the 4 loudest; it can be turned off in Settings.\n- **Scan** (aim mode): a ring expands from you to 40 m in 0.6 s. Every Whiteout it touches is revealed for 6 s\n  (+0.4 s a Steady level). Cooldown 1.2 s. When revealed and within 30 m, the warm spot shows: an orange-red glow\n  (`world.glow`) plus a pulsing diamond ring in the HUD.\n- Revealing fades the figure in over 0.25 s with a static flicker. Unrevealing fades it out over 0.4 s.\n- Skills that reveal too: Ansel's Flare (all within 30 m for 8 s), Kasimir's Echo (marks through walls for 5 s), and\n  Mireille's Flash (reveals what is in its cone).\n\n**Tests:** an unrevealed enemy has `visible = false` and still takes hits; a scan reveals exactly the enemies within\nthe ring's radius at the time it passes them; the reveal runs out after 6 s + Steady; footprints are emitted along the\npath at stride length; the laugh rate rises as distance falls.\n\n### 7.6 Whiteouts: behaviour, spawns, waves (`30-whiteouts.js`)\n\n| Type | HP | Speed | Contact | Red (body / crit) | Rime (crit) | Behaviour |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","numLines":150,"startLine":499,"totalLines":2115}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KyrsbCmtGTp8VqvPPktN5e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
