{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2g16QSpbrxQwH9e5pU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AVFAsHcWd6wmWvWvF5JVSG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":797,"limit":140},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7564,"cache_read_input_tokens":498066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7564},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"a58493ae-0378-440d-9387-21f924e32e89","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:39.707Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2fzonqtoxVP45AtEBM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AVFAsHcWd6wmWvWvF5JVSG":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":797,"limit":140}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVFAsHcWd6wmWvWvF5JVSG","type":"tool_result","content":"797\t### 7.14 NPCs and hints (`51-npcs.js`)\n798\t\n799\t- **Murmel** (three spots: 00A reception, 01A ski school, 01C top station). Interact: a hint picked from a table by\n800\t  the current objective (§11.9). The first hint is free; each one after costs 10 Red (free for Rurik). The menu shows\n801\t  \"BUY A HINT (10 RED)\" and \"LEAVE\".\n802\t- **Pim the Lift Boy** (§11.9): a translucent ghost on a floating chairlift seat that rocks gently. His appearances\n803\t  are fixed; each gives lore and a nudge.\n804\t- **Telephones** (a booth or a house phone, ringing as you near): the Concierge's calls, once each. Each is a story beat.\n805\t- **Frozen tableaux** (01A villagers, 01B delegates, 01E deposits): rigs frozen mid-gesture in ice. Check gives a\n806\t  line.\n807\t- **Sister Rosalind** (Room 7) states the current objective in her own words. **Oma Holle** gives one line per visit,\n808\t  from a list that changes with progress.\n809\t\n810\t**Tests:** hints cost 10 (0 for Rurik) and depend on the objective; each phone call fires once; Rosalind's objective\n811\tline matches `S7.objective()`.\n812\t\n813\t### 7.15 Story, dialogue, cutscenes, title cards (`50-story.js`)\n814\t\n815\t- One `E.Story` (people, nodes, vars) talking through one `E.Dialog` (`lines: 3`, `voice: null`; our voice synth types\n816\t  along, §10.4). `people` maps speaker ids to names, portrait rigs (live `rig.drawPortrait`) and voices.\n817\t- **Presentation:** a bottom box at about 70% of the screen width; the name in red capitals; text at scale 2. When a\n818\t  line starts, the speaker's name card pops in big for 0.4 s; it shows whenever the speaker changes.\n819\t- **Title cards** (`G.card`): a black screen, the white title at scale 4–5 (`E.font.title`, ink outline), a red\n820\t  subtitle, the target's black silhouette portrait (`rig.drawPortrait` tinted black), and a sting. Hard cut in, 2.5 s,\n821\t  hard cut out (any button skips after 0.8 s).\n822\t- **Cutscenes** are beats with letterbox bars (12% top and bottom), director overrides, rigs driven by `anim` poses and\n823\t  tweens. Start or Pause opens \"Skip scene? YES / NO\".\n824\t- **Objectives:** `S7.objective()` returns one line from the story flags (for example \"Ring for service on the third\n825\t  floor.\"). It shows in the map screen and through Rosalind. There is no HUD objective marker; the map and the hints\n826\t  do that job.\n827\t- **Tutorials:** one-shot tips with big glyphs (\"HOLD ✕ TO WALK\"). Each clears when its action is done, and its flag is\n828\t  saved. Pause → Help (an E.Shell `help` screen) lists the keys for the last device and short sections on how to play.\n829\t\n830\t**Tests:** every node referenced by an area or beat exists (the validator); a cold-open run (the bot pressing confirm)\n831\treaches play; story state round-trips through a save; skipping a cutscene lands in the same state as watching it.\n832\t\n833\t### 7.16 Room 7 (`52-room7.js`, `content/areas/room7.js`)\n834\t\n835\t- **Every area has a Room 7 door:** a plain door with a frosted stencilled \"7\". Interact: the screen whites out in a\n836\t  flurry (0.6 s) and you stand inside Room 7. Leaving returns you to the door you came through. The area's world stays\n837\t  in memory, frozen.\n838\t- **Inside** (one persistent world; a rail loop of 6 stops):\n839\t  - the **Door**;\n840\t  - the **Cuckoo Clock**: save (`game.saves.show('save')`; `saves.canSave` is true only in Room 7);\n841\t  - the **Wax Bench**: upgrades;\n842\t  - the **Wardrobe**: seven coats, persona select, the Sweep included;\n843\t  - the **Bed**: Oma Holle's line;\n844\t  - the **Window**: the current area's view as a postcard of falling snow, plus the area's Lift Pin count.\n845\t  Sister Rosalind knits in an armchair by the bed (talk: the objective). The telephone on the side table replays the\n846\t  current briefing.\n847\t- Music: a music-box waltz (§10.1). Entering autosaves.\n848\t\n849\t**Tests:** entering and leaving returns you to the same door; the clock saves to a slot; the Wardrobe can pick the\n850\tSweep; doors refuse while enemies are alive.\n851\t\n852\t### 7.17 Saves and checkpoints (`60-save.js`)\n853\t\n854\t- `game.saves` (3 slots plus the autosave; `menu: { saves: { slots: 3, version: 1, migrate } }`). Save data is\n855\t  `{ v: 1, area, node, dir, persona, roster: { id: { hp, stats, frozen, statue, unlocked } }, red, rime, items, pins,\n856\t  opened gates, dead waves, collected spots, story: story.state(), results, playtime, difficulty }`. Place: the area's\n857\t  title. Level: \"TARGET 00\" or \"TARGET 01\".\n858\t- **Autosave:** on area entry, on Room 7 entry, and at every boss start (as the boss checkpoint). Never during a session\n859\t  (the hub's storage is empty anyway) or during attract mode or bot tests (unless a test asks).\n860\t- **Title:** CONTINUE loads `game.saves.latest()`; LOAD opens `saves.show('load')`.\n861\t\n862\t**Tests:** serialize → deserialize → serialize is byte-equal; a save made mid-area restores the walker, roster, items,\n863\tflags and opened gates; a version-0 save is migrated or refused cleanly.\n864\t\n865\t### 7.18 Map (`82-screens.js`)\n866\t\n867\tPause → Map, or Create / M in rail mode. A schematic of the current area's rail graph: visited edges as thick white\n868\tlines, unvisited but seen edges dotted, nodes as dots. Icons: Room 7 doors (a 7), Murmel, Pim, phones, gates (a lock\n869\tand the solver's face; struck through once opened), exits (an arrow and the destination's name), collected and\n870\tmissing pickups that you have seen, your persona's portrait at your position, and frozen statues (an ice icon).\n871\tL1/R1 cycles visited areas. The objective line sits at the bottom. It is big and sparse: never more than 20 icons.\n872\t\n873\t### 7.19 HUD (`81-hud.js`)\n874\t\n875\tMinimal, like Killer7. Every piece is inside the 5% safe margin.\n876\t- **Top left:** the persona's portrait (32 px), their name at scale 2, the HP bar (80×5; white, recent damage in\n877\t  red), and the Red thermos (a vertical 6×30 vial; it drains while healing).\n878\t- **Top right:** Rime (a crystal icon and a count). In Target 01, the three Edelweiss slots.\n879\t- **Bottom centre:** context prompts (§6.2). The junction label of the highlighted branch.\n880\t- **Aim mode:** the persona's reticle at the centre (or at the pointer), ammo pips under it, the scan cooldown as a\n881\t  ring round it, warm-spot diamonds, laugh ripples, damage chevrons, the scope vignette for Long Look, \"RELOADING\"\n882\t  as a thin bar.\n883\t- **Splashes:** THAW. · TOO FAR. · CRITICAL BRAVO (bosses) · RED +n.\n884\t- **Statue marker** while rescuing: a direction arrow and metres.\n885\t- **Hidden** in cutscenes, in Room 7 (except the prompts) and with the dev toggle.\n886\t\n887\t### 7.20 Menus and screens (`82-screens.js`, `83-shell.js`)\n888\t\n889\t- **Title** (canvas over the Room 7 world: the camera drifts slowly over the bed toward the snowing window). The\n890\t  \"SKILLER7\" logo uses `E.font.title` at scale 5 (white, a red \"7\", an ink outline). Entries: NEW GAME · CONTINUE\n891\t  (only with a save) · LOAD · ECHO RUN · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Version and build at the bottom. Idle for 10 s →\n892\t  attract.\n893\t- **New Game** asks for the difficulty (Bunny Hill / Piste / Off-Piste), one line each, then the cold open.\n894\t- **Pause** (the engine's E.Shell, themed): Resume · Map · Items & Dossier · Personas (the seven cards: portrait, name,\n895\t  weapon, skill, stats, HP, status; read-only outside Room 7) · Help · About & Credits · Dev Mode · Settings ·\n896\t  Controls · Full screen · Quit to title. Custom items come from `menu.items`, a function, so a session can drop Dev Mode and Quit. An item's\n897\t  callback closes the Shell (`shell.hide()`) and opens our canvas modal.\n898\t- **Room 7 screens:** the Wax Bench, the Wardrobe (the seven coats in a row; the focused one large with its card).\n899\t- **Results** (after each target): the rank badge (Green Circle / Blue Square / Black Diamond / Double Black) and six\n900\t  stats (time, Whiteouts thawed, crit %, Red collected, personas frozen, hints bought) with the Concierge's one-line\n901\t  note.\n902\t- **Game over**, the **target cards**, the **code lock**, the **touch-only notice**, the **attract overlay** (\"DEMO ·\n903\t  PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with a glyph-aware button name).\n904\t- **About & Credits** (from the title and from the pause menu): pages of large text holding the Source Information fields,\n905\t  Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback exactly as written in the hand-back (§16), then the credits:\n906\t  \"Made with my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module (MIT) · three.js r182 (MIT) · Rapier 0.19.3 (Apache-2.0) · AI Hub\n907\t  session client 1.4.0 · Asset store entries converted from Kenney and KayKit CC0 sets\" (list only the sets actually\n908\t  used) · \"Inspired by Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005). An original game; no affiliation.\"\n909\t- E.Shell theme: `{ ink: '#f4f1ea', paper: '#0b0a0c', accent: '#d81e2a', muted: '#8a8590', danger: '#ff3a3a',\n910\t  line: '#2a262c', font: '600 22px \"Arial Narrow\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif',\n911\t  titleFont: '900 44px Impact, \"Arial Black\", sans-serif' }`.\n912\t\n913\t### 7.21 Settings\n914\t\n915\tEngine standard (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller, Touch) plus the 3D settings `picture3d` (default `pixels`),\n916\t`shadows3d` (on) and `filter3d` (default **cel**). Define these three ourselves in `menu.settings`, with the same keys\n917\tand options as `E.World3D.SETTINGS` but our defaults, so they also exist headless. A world reads them when it is made\n918\tand follows any change. Never pass `res` or `filter.look` to a new world: world options override the player's choice.\n919\t`look3d` (cards or puppets) is left out: our hats, accessories and weapons are drawn on cards, so characters are always\n920\tcards. Our group **Game:**\n921\t\n922\t| Key | Options | Default |\n923\t|---|---|---|\n924\t| `difficulty` | Bunny Hill · Piste · Off-Piste | Piste (changeable mid-game) |\n925\t| `aimToggle` | Hold · Toggle | Hold |\n926\t| `aimAssist` | Off · Low · High | Low |\n927\t| `padSens` | slider 0.5–2.0 | 1.0 |\n928\t| `mouseMode` | Look · Pointer | Look |\n929\t| `mouseSens` | slider 0.03–0.4 °/px | 0.12 |\n930\t| `laughCues` | On · Off (HUD ripples) | On |\n931\t| `textSize` | Normal · Large (dialog at scale 2 or 3) | Normal |\n932\t| `voices` | slider 0–1 | 0.8 |\n933\t| `padGlyphs` | PlayStation · Xbox (writes the engine's `glyphs`) | PlayStation |\n934\t\n935\t### 7.22 Dev mode (`84-dev.js`)\n936\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"e0150a95-726a-4b66-969c-6ef19817b5b0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:39.713Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 7.14 NPCs and hints (`51-npcs.js`)\n\n- **Murmel** (three spots: 00A reception, 01A ski school, 01C top station). Interact: a hint picked from a table by\n  the current objective (§11.9). The first hint is free; each one after costs 10 Red (free for Rurik). The menu shows\n  \"BUY A HINT (10 RED)\" and \"LEAVE\".\n- **Pim the Lift Boy** (§11.9): a translucent ghost on a floating chairlift seat that rocks gently. His appearances\n  are fixed; each gives lore and a nudge.\n- **Telephones** (a booth or a house phone, ringing as you near): the Concierge's calls, once each. Each is a story beat.\n- **Frozen tableaux** (01A villagers, 01B delegates, 01E deposits): rigs frozen mid-gesture in ice. Check gives a\n  line.\n- **Sister Rosalind** (Room 7) states the current objective in her own words. **Oma Holle** gives one line per visit,\n  from a list that changes with progress.\n\n**Tests:** hints cost 10 (0 for Rurik) and depend on the objective; each phone call fires once; Rosalind's objective\nline matches `S7.objective()`.\n\n### 7.15 Story, dialogue, cutscenes, title cards (`50-story.js`)\n\n- One `E.Story` (people, nodes, vars) talking through one `E.Dialog` (`lines: 3`, `voice: null`; our voice synth types\n  along, §10.4). `people` maps speaker ids to names, portrait rigs (live `rig.drawPortrait`) and voices.\n- **Presentation:** a bottom box at about 70% of the screen width; the name in red capitals; text at scale 2. When a\n  line starts, the speaker's name card pops in big for 0.4 s; it shows whenever the speaker changes.\n- **Title cards** (`G.card`): a black screen, the white title at scale 4–5 (`E.font.title`, ink outline), a red\n  subtitle, the target's black silhouette portrait (`rig.drawPortrait` tinted black), and a sting. Hard cut in, 2.5 s,\n  hard cut out (any button skips after 0.8 s).\n- **Cutscenes** are beats with letterbox bars (12% top and bottom), director overrides, rigs driven by `anim` poses and\n  tweens. Start or Pause opens \"Skip scene? YES / NO\".\n- **Objectives:** `S7.objective()` returns one line from the story flags (for example \"Ring for service on the third\n  floor.\"). It shows in the map screen and through Rosalind. There is no HUD objective marker; the map and the hints\n  do that job.\n- **Tutorials:** one-shot tips with big glyphs (\"HOLD ✕ TO WALK\"). Each clears when its action is done, and its flag is\n  saved. Pause → Help (an E.Shell `help` screen) lists the keys for the last device and short sections on how to play.\n\n**Tests:** every node referenced by an area or beat exists (the validator); a cold-open run (the bot pressing confirm)\nreaches play; story state round-trips through a save; skipping a cutscene lands in the same state as watching it.\n\n### 7.16 Room 7 (`52-room7.js`, `content/areas/room7.js`)\n\n- **Every area has a Room 7 door:** a plain door with a frosted stencilled \"7\". Interact: the screen whites out in a\n  flurry (0.6 s) and you stand inside Room 7. Leaving returns you to the door you came through. The area's world stays\n  in memory, frozen.\n- **Inside** (one persistent world; a rail loop of 6 stops):\n  - the **Door**;\n  - the **Cuckoo Clock**: save (`game.saves.show('save')`; `saves.canSave` is true only in Room 7);\n  - the **Wax Bench**: upgrades;\n  - the **Wardrobe**: seven coats, persona select, the Sweep included;\n  - the **Bed**: Oma Holle's line;\n  - the **Window**: the current area's view as a postcard of falling snow, plus the area's Lift Pin count.\n  Sister Rosalind knits in an armchair by the bed (talk: the objective). The telephone on the side table replays the\n  current briefing.\n- Music: a music-box waltz (§10.1). Entering autosaves.\n\n**Tests:** entering and leaving returns you to the same door; the clock saves to a slot; the Wardrobe can pick the\nSweep; doors refuse while enemies are alive.\n\n### 7.17 Saves and checkpoints (`60-save.js`)\n\n- `game.saves` (3 slots plus the autosave; `menu: { saves: { slots: 3, version: 1, migrate } }`). Save data is\n  `{ v: 1, area, node, dir, persona, roster: { id: { hp, stats, frozen, statue, unlocked } }, red, rime, items, pins,\n  opened gates, dead waves, collected spots, story: story.state(), results, playtime, difficulty }`. Place: the area's\n  title. Level: \"TARGET 00\" or \"TARGET 01\".\n- **Autosave:** on area entry, on Room 7 entry, and at every boss start (as the boss checkpoint). Never during a session\n  (the hub's storage is empty anyway) or during attract mode or bot tests (unless a test asks).\n- **Title:** CONTINUE loads `game.saves.latest()`; LOAD opens `saves.show('load')`.\n\n**Tests:** serialize → deserialize → serialize is byte-equal; a save made mid-area restores the walker, roster, items,\nflags and opened gates; a version-0 save is migrated or refused cleanly.\n\n### 7.18 Map (`82-screens.js`)\n\nPause → Map, or Create / M in rail mode. A schematic of the current area's rail graph: visited edges as thick white\nlines, unvisited but seen edges dotted, nodes as dots. Icons: Room 7 doors (a 7), Murmel, Pim, phones, gates (a lock\nand the solver's face; struck through once opened), exits (an arrow and the destination's name), collected and\nmissing pickups that you have seen, your persona's portrait at your position, and frozen statues (an ice icon).\nL1/R1 cycles visited areas. The objective line sits at the bottom. It is big and sparse: never more than 20 icons.\n\n### 7.19 HUD (`81-hud.js`)\n\nMinimal, like Killer7. Every piece is inside the 5% safe margin.\n- **Top left:** the persona's portrait (32 px), their name at scale 2, the HP bar (80×5; white, recent damage in\n  red), and the Red thermos (a vertical 6×30 vial; it drains while healing).\n- **Top right:** Rime (a crystal icon and a count). In Target 01, the three Edelweiss slots.\n- **Bottom centre:** context prompts (§6.2). The junction label of the highlighted branch.\n- **Aim mode:** the persona's reticle at the centre (or at the pointer), ammo pips under it, the scan cooldown as a\n  ring round it, warm-spot diamonds, laugh ripples, damage chevrons, the scope vignette for Long Look, \"RELOADING\"\n  as a thin bar.\n- **Splashes:** THAW. · TOO FAR. · CRITICAL BRAVO (bosses) · RED +n.\n- **Statue marker** while rescuing: a direction arrow and metres.\n- **Hidden** in cutscenes, in Room 7 (except the prompts) and with the dev toggle.\n\n### 7.20 Menus and screens (`82-screens.js`, `83-shell.js`)\n\n- **Title** (canvas over the Room 7 world: the camera drifts slowly over the bed toward the snowing window). The\n  \"SKILLER7\" logo uses `E.font.title` at scale 5 (white, a red \"7\", an ink outline). Entries: NEW GAME · CONTINUE\n  (only with a save) · LOAD · ECHO RUN · SETTINGS · ABOUT & CREDITS. Version and build at the bottom. Idle for 10 s →\n  attract.\n- **New Game** asks for the difficulty (Bunny Hill / Piste / Off-Piste), one line each, then the cold open.\n- **Pause** (the engine's E.Shell, themed): Resume · Map · Items & Dossier · Personas (the seven cards: portrait, name,\n  weapon, skill, stats, HP, status; read-only outside Room 7) · Help · About & Credits · Dev Mode · Settings ·\n  Controls · Full screen · Quit to title. Custom items come from `menu.items`, a function, so a session can drop Dev Mode and Quit. An item's\n  callback closes the Shell (`shell.hide()`) and opens our canvas modal.\n- **Room 7 screens:** the Wax Bench, the Wardrobe (the seven coats in a row; the focused one large with its card).\n- **Results** (after each target): the rank badge (Green Circle / Blue Square / Black Diamond / Double Black) and six\n  stats (time, Whiteouts thawed, crit %, Red collected, personas frozen, hints bought) with the Concierge's one-line\n  note.\n- **Game over**, the **target cards**, the **code lock**, the **touch-only notice**, the **attract overlay** (\"DEMO ·\n  PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with a glyph-aware button name).\n- **About & Credits** (from the title and from the pause menu): pages of large text holding the Source Information fields,\n  Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback exactly as written in the hand-back (§16), then the credits:\n  \"Made with my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module (MIT) · three.js r182 (MIT) · Rapier 0.19.3 (Apache-2.0) · AI Hub\n  session client 1.4.0 · Asset store entries converted from Kenney and KayKit CC0 sets\" (list only the sets actually\n  used) · \"Inspired by Killer7 (Grasshopper Manufacture / Capcom, 2005). An original game; no affiliation.\"\n- E.Shell theme: `{ ink: '#f4f1ea', paper: '#0b0a0c', accent: '#d81e2a', muted: '#8a8590', danger: '#ff3a3a',\n  line: '#2a262c', font: '600 22px \"Arial Narrow\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif',\n  titleFont: '900 44px Impact, \"Arial Black\", sans-serif' }`.\n\n### 7.21 Settings\n\nEngine standard (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller, Touch) plus the 3D settings `picture3d` (default `pixels`),\n`shadows3d` (on) and `filter3d` (default **cel**). Define these three ourselves in `menu.settings`, with the same keys\nand options as `E.World3D.SETTINGS` but our defaults, so they also exist headless. A world reads them when it is made\nand follows any change. Never pass `res` or `filter.look` to a new world: world options override the player's choice.\n`look3d` (cards or puppets) is left out: our hats, accessories and weapons are drawn on cards, so characters are always\ncards. Our group **Game:**\n\n| Key | Options | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `difficulty` | Bunny Hill · Piste · Off-Piste | Piste (changeable mid-game) |\n| `aimToggle` | Hold · Toggle | Hold |\n| `aimAssist` | Off · Low · High | Low |\n| `padSens` | slider 0.5–2.0 | 1.0 |\n| `mouseMode` | Look · Pointer | Look |\n| `mouseSens` | slider 0.03–0.4 °/px | 0.12 |\n| `laughCues` | On · Off (HUD ripples) | On |\n| `textSize` | Normal · Large (dialog at scale 2 or 3) | Normal |\n| `voices` | slider 0–1 | 0.8 |\n| `padGlyphs` | PlayStation · Xbox (writes the engine's `glyphs`) | PlayStation |\n\n### 7.22 Dev mode (`84-dev.js`)\n","numLines":140,"startLine":797,"totalLines":2115}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AVFAsHcWd6wmWvWvF5JVSG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
