{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2gNEPg4uaQziTPi7wB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014XmvqyhSdRGH8Cf6cFVT4a","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":936,"limit":130},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4762,"cache_read_input_tokens":505630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4762},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"47f3725e-ee1c-4e9d-a810-1d43ca1229b5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:44.811Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2gMyWTXM897e5De1Hx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014XmvqyhSdRGH8Cf6cFVT4a":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":936,"limit":130}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XmvqyhSdRGH8Cf6cFVT4a","type":"tool_result","content":"936\t\n937\t**Pause → Dev Mode** opens a canvas modal (the sim frozen behind it, half-dimmed). Pages switch with L1/R1 or Q/E.\n938\tUp/down picks, left/right adjusts (hold to repeat), △ / Backspace resets the focused value, □ / Delete **resets the\n939\tpage to defaults** (it asks first), ○ / Esc closes. The mouse hovers and drags sliders. Values apply live (the moment\n940\tyou close it, the game runs with them) and are saved in `localStorage['s7:dev']`. There is a **Reset all to defaults**\n941\tbutton at the top of every page.\n942\t\n943\t| Page | Contents |\n944\t|---|---|\n945\t| **Tuning** (sliders) | walk speed (85; 40–200) · ski top speed (190; 100–400) · aim sensitivity (pad; 0.5–2) · aim assist strength (0–1) · enemy speed × (1; 0.3–2) · enemy HP × (1; 0.2–3) · player damage × (1; 0.2–3) · warm spot radius × (1; 0.5–2.5) · scan radius (40 m; 10–80) · reveal time (6 s; 1–15) · spawn rate × (1; 0.3–2) · explosion damage × (1; 0–3) · Red drop × (1; 0–3) · Rime drop × (1; 0–3) · heal rate (40; 10–200) · time scale (1; 0.1–2) · cel bands (3; 2–8) · ink strength (1; 0–1.5) · fog far × (1; 0.3–3) |\n946\t| **Cheats** (toggles) | god mode · infinite Red · one-hit kills · reveal all · ghost through gates · all personas · show rails and nodes · show hit volumes and warm spots · show camera shots (frusta and ids) · free camera (fly: the left stick or WASD, the right stick or mouse, Q/E up and down) · hide HUD · slow motion on crits · show FPS and sim hash |\n947\t| **Warp** | every area → every node (lists of up to 7, paged) · start any boss or boss phase · jump to any story beat · give items (3 Edelweiss, Service Key, Ember Charm, all pins) · +100 Red · +20 Rime · revive all · kill all · trigger any wave · freeze the active persona (to test the rescue) |\n948\t| **Info** | area, edge and s, shot id, mode, alive and revealed enemies, sim hash, seed, version, build date, backend (WebGPU / WebGL 2) |\n949\t\n950\tHidden in AI Hub sessions. Its overlays (rails, volumes, shots) draw with `world.pen` lines and boxes.\n951\t\n952\t**Tests:** every slider applies (set → snapshot shows the effect); reset restores every default; the free camera\n953\tdoesn't move the sim; warps land on the named node.\n954\t\n955\t### 7.23 Attract mode (`86-attract.js`, `content/attract.js`)\n956\t\n957\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any title submenu (Echo Run setup, About, the touch-only notice; the\n958\t  timer also counts while an engine Settings screen is open over the title, from real time in `draw`).\n959\t- **What plays:** a loop of seven vignettes (§11.12), each 18–25 s, each opening with a caption card. A cheating bot\n960\t  plays them: god mode, infinite Red, instant warps between vignettes, aim that snaps to warm spots, reveal all. It\n961\t  shows rails, aiming, scanning, crits, persona switching, the ring, skills, the lifts, the avalanche, the gondola,\n962\t  both bosses' set pieces and Room 7.\n963\t- **Overlay:** the small SKILLER7 logo top left, \"DEMO\" top right, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" at the bottom (glyph-aware).\n964\t- **Exit:** any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse move over 6 px, gamepad button, stick past the dead zone, or touch. Then\n965\t  `game.input.consumeAll()`, a flurry back to the title, and the idle timer resets. The input that exits never\n966\t  activates a menu item.\n967\t- **Determinism:** seeded. Headless, it runs the full loop with no errors (§14).\n968\t\n969\t### 7.24 Multiplayer: AI Hub session and Echo Run (`87-hub.js`, `88-echorun.js`)\n970\t\n971\t**Echo Run** is the Black Run (01C) as a time trial: you play as Dagny from the start gate to the village. Whiteout\n972\tencounters sit at fixed distances with seeded types and warm spots. A Whiteout that reaches you adds **+3 s** and a\n973\tstumble. Each crit takes **0.5 s** off. Three routes: BLUE (safe), BLACK (fast, but with Plows), and THE JUMP (the\n974\tfastest). Ranks: Double Black < 95 s · Black < 110 s · Blue < 130 s · else Green.\n975\t\n976\t**On its own (no hub):** Echo Run from the title. Your best run is recorded (walker edge, s, aim state and persona\n977\tevery 0.1 s, about 1,200 samples) in `localStorage['s7:echo']` and replayed as **YOUR ECHO**: a translucent rig in\n978\tpale blue with a name tag. Results show your best time and rank. The campaign itself is single-player. In an AI Hub\n979\tsession the same mode runs over the network (below).\n980\t\n981\t**In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`):\n982\t1. At start, skip the title, attract mode and menus. Boot builds the Black Run world, then\n983\t   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] })`. If it returns `null`, carry on as the normal game.\n984\t2. Seed the course from `AIHub.rng('course')`. Show \"GET READY\" over the start gate, and call `AIHub.ready()` with no\n985\t   key press. We use the hub's own card (no `card: true`).\n986\t3. On `start`, count 3-2-1 against `AIHub.time()`. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n987\t4. **Send** (unreliable, 10 Hz): `{ t: 'g', area: 'blackrun', e: edgeIndex, s: Math.round(s), a: aiming ? 1 : 0,\n988\t   y: Math.round(yaw * 100) }`. When you finish, send reliably: `{ t: 'done', time }`.\n989\t5. **Receive:** draw each other player as an **echo**: a translucent rig (`actor.fade = .45`) with a scarf in their\n990\t   seat colour (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) and a name tag above (from `world.project`; names are\n991\t   drawn as text, never inserted as HTML). Positions ease toward the latest sample. Echoes affect nothing.\n992\t6. **Progress** about once a second: `AIHub.progress({ score: metresDown, label: '62% down · +6 s' })`.\n993\t7. **Finish:** `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time() + penaltyMs), stats: { Crits, Penalties, Thawed },\n994\t   awards: [{ title: 'Clean Line', detail: 'No penalties' }] })`, once. Then wait, watching the echoes.\n995\t8. **`time-up`:** if you haven't finished, `AIHub.result({ score: metresDown })` at once.\n996\t9. **`end`:** stop input (`game.input.clear()`, ignore everything) and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, stop the\n997\t   music), freeze the sim, and show \"ROUND OVER\". The hub shows the results.\n998\t10. **`leave`:** remove that player's echo.\n999\t11. **Session rules:** no Quit, no Dev Mode, no saves, no map (Create stays free for the hub's Create + Options); the\n1000\t    pause menu keeps Resume, Settings, Controls and Help; no `alert` or `confirm`, no new windows or links, no network\n1001\t    other than the hub; ignore Options while Create is held (§5.9). On a touch-only device, `AIHub.fail` (§6.5).\n1002\t\n1003\t**Tests:** the harness (§14.5) with players=2 auto; players=4 with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5; the host-leave\n1004\tscenario. Also the game outside a session (`AIHub.active` false): the title appears and Echo Run plays solo with your\n1005\techo.\n1006\t\n1007\t### 7.25 Difficulty, ranks, accessibility\n1008\t\n1009\t| | Bunny Hill | Piste | Off-Piste |\n1010\t|---|---|---|---|\n1011\t| Enemy damage | ×0.5 | ×1 | ×1.5 |\n1012\t| Enemy speed | ×0.85 | ×1 | ×1.15 |\n1013\t| Reveal time | ×1.5 | ×1 | ×0.7 |\n1014\t| Red drops | ×1.3 | ×1 | ×0.8 |\n1015\t| Aim assist default | High | Low | Off |\n1016\t| Avalanche speed | ×0.85 | ×1 | ×1.1 |\n1017\t\n1018\t**Target ranks:** Double Black: crit % ≥ 60, no persona frozen, time ≤ par (Target 00 par 12 min, Target 01 par\n1019\t40 min). Black: crit % ≥ 40 and at most 1 frozen. Blue: crit % ≥ 20. Otherwise Green.\n1020\t\n1021\t**Accessibility:** laugh ripples, warm-spot diamonds, every line subtitled (the voices are gibberish anyway), text\n1022\tsize, hold or toggle aim, aim assist, the engine's comfort settings (reduce motion, shake, flashes) respected by every\n1023\teffect, rumble from the engine's vibration setting, and no colour-only information.\n1024\t\n1025\t---\n1026\t\n1027\t## 8. Art direction and rendering\n1028\t\n1029\t### 8.1 The look\n1030\t\n1031\t- **The engine's native style:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand`, the 3D picture at `'pixels'` (the game's own resolution,\n1032\t  chunky; the `picture3d` setting), characters as **cards** (rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's angle), plus the\n1033\t  3D module's **Comic cel** filter (the `filter3d` setting's default; per world `bands: 3, ink: 1, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.4,\n1034\t  apply: 'all'`). Light falls in a few flat bands, ink traces edges and silhouettes, colours are pushed.\n1035\t- **Killer7's feel, made ours:** large flat areas of white snow and black shadow; one accent colour per area; harsh\n1036\t  single key lights and long shadows (the sun or moon with shadows outdoors, a spot or strong point light indoors);\n1037\t  saturated **red** only for blood-red things (Red, wounds, the logo, the focus bar). White Whiteouts on white snow are\n1038\t  made readable by the ink.\n1039\t- **Typography:** chunky capitals, big, centred, hard cuts. Every chapter and boss gets a title card.\n1040\t- Run `node engine/tools/check.mjs` (with the CDN routed, §14.4) for its notes on contrast and screen fill, and act on\n1041\t  them where they apply to a 3D game.\n1042\t\n1043\t### 8.2 Palettes and lighting per area\n1044\t\n1045\t| Area | Accent | Key light | Fill and fog | Notes |\n1046\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1047\t| Room 7 | candle amber | one hanging lamp (warm), the window's moonlight (cold) | `#1a1418`, fog off | the window always snows |\n1048\t| 00A Lobby | oxblood and brass | 3 chandeliers (`#ffd8a0`), moonlight through the revolving door | `#1a1012` | marble checker floor, red runner |\n1049\t| 00B Third floor | sick green-white | sconces, one failing (flicker .6) | `#0c100c`, near fog | long corridor sightlines |\n1050\t| 00C Shaft | emergency red | a red rotating beacon, the car's own light | `#100406` | vertical space |\n1051\t| 01A Village | Glühwein red and candle gold | dusk sun low in the west with shadows; string lights; stall fires (torches) | sky `#2a2440 → #e8a070` | snow ground, timber chalets |\n1052\t| 01B Palais | committee blue and grey | cold fluorescent panels (several white lights), flag uplights | `#0a0c14` | marble, glass, flags |\n1053\t| 01C Black Run | course orange (piste poles) | floodlights along the piste, the moon | night `#05070f` | orange nets, black signs |\n1054\t| 01D Gondola | steel blue and sodium orange | the moon, the cabin's interior light, pylon lamps | storm fog | cable lines against the sky |\n1055\t| 01E Archive | glacier cyan | cyan glows from the ice (`world.glow`, light: true) | `#02060a`, close fog | frozen people in the walls |\n1056\t| 01F Summit | violet night and Föhn amber | starlight, an amber glow from the pavilion that warms as the boss nears the end | clears from storm to stars | dripping icicles |\n1057\t\n1058\t### 8.3 Characters (rig specs; `E.Humanoid`, `size: 1.3` unless stated, `look: 'card'`)\n1059\t\n1060\t| Who | build | outfit, hair, hat | acc | weapon | colours |\n1061\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1062\t| Ansel | heroic, hunch .15 | coat; short `#9a9aa0`; beanie `#18181c`, pom `#f06a1e` | goggles (amber) on the forehead, pack (red, white stripe) | revolver | skin `#e6c8b0` coat/cloth `#d2461e` pants `#1c1c22` boot `#2a2420` trim `#f4f4f4` |\n1063\t| Dagny | heroic | shirt (a speed suit); ponytail `#f0d890`; racehelmet `#c0c8d0`, visor `#ff8a1e` | — | poles | cloth and pants `#1e5cff`, trim `#ffffff`, boot `#101014` |\n1064\t| Ignaz | heroic, hunch .1 | coat; short `#e8e8e8`; felt `#2e4a2a`, feather `#e8e0c0` | moustache `#f0f0f0` | rifle | coat `#7a5a3a` pants `#6a4a2a` boot `#8a1a1a` (red socks) trim `#3a2a1a` |\n1065\t| Rurik | bulky, size 1.4 | coat (fur); short `#1a1410`; ushanka `#4a3a2a` | beard `#1a1410`, cigar | shotgun (gold) | coat `#3a2a20` trim `#d8b040` pants `#141416` |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"c7ebdd9c-fffa-4b14-8e51-15ea9fc85e5e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:44.817Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Pause → Dev Mode** opens a canvas modal (the sim frozen behind it, half-dimmed). Pages switch with L1/R1 or Q/E.\nUp/down picks, left/right adjusts (hold to repeat), △ / Backspace resets the focused value, □ / Delete **resets the\npage to defaults** (it asks first), ○ / Esc closes. The mouse hovers and drags sliders. Values apply live (the moment\nyou close it, the game runs with them) and are saved in `localStorage['s7:dev']`. There is a **Reset all to defaults**\nbutton at the top of every page.\n\n| Page | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| **Tuning** (sliders) | walk speed (85; 40–200) · ski top speed (190; 100–400) · aim sensitivity (pad; 0.5–2) · aim assist strength (0–1) · enemy speed × (1; 0.3–2) · enemy HP × (1; 0.2–3) · player damage × (1; 0.2–3) · warm spot radius × (1; 0.5–2.5) · scan radius (40 m; 10–80) · reveal time (6 s; 1–15) · spawn rate × (1; 0.3–2) · explosion damage × (1; 0–3) · Red drop × (1; 0–3) · Rime drop × (1; 0–3) · heal rate (40; 10–200) · time scale (1; 0.1–2) · cel bands (3; 2–8) · ink strength (1; 0–1.5) · fog far × (1; 0.3–3) |\n| **Cheats** (toggles) | god mode · infinite Red · one-hit kills · reveal all · ghost through gates · all personas · show rails and nodes · show hit volumes and warm spots · show camera shots (frusta and ids) · free camera (fly: the left stick or WASD, the right stick or mouse, Q/E up and down) · hide HUD · slow motion on crits · show FPS and sim hash |\n| **Warp** | every area → every node (lists of up to 7, paged) · start any boss or boss phase · jump to any story beat · give items (3 Edelweiss, Service Key, Ember Charm, all pins) · +100 Red · +20 Rime · revive all · kill all · trigger any wave · freeze the active persona (to test the rescue) |\n| **Info** | area, edge and s, shot id, mode, alive and revealed enemies, sim hash, seed, version, build date, backend (WebGPU / WebGL 2) |\n\nHidden in AI Hub sessions. Its overlays (rails, volumes, shots) draw with `world.pen` lines and boxes.\n\n**Tests:** every slider applies (set → snapshot shows the effect); reset restores every default; the free camera\ndoesn't move the sim; warps land on the named node.\n\n### 7.23 Attract mode (`86-attract.js`, `content/attract.js`)\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any title submenu (Echo Run setup, About, the touch-only notice; the\n  timer also counts while an engine Settings screen is open over the title, from real time in `draw`).\n- **What plays:** a loop of seven vignettes (§11.12), each 18–25 s, each opening with a caption card. A cheating bot\n  plays them: god mode, infinite Red, instant warps between vignettes, aim that snaps to warm spots, reveal all. It\n  shows rails, aiming, scanning, crits, persona switching, the ring, skills, the lifts, the avalanche, the gondola,\n  both bosses' set pieces and Room 7.\n- **Overlay:** the small SKILLER7 logo top left, \"DEMO\" top right, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" at the bottom (glyph-aware).\n- **Exit:** any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse move over 6 px, gamepad button, stick past the dead zone, or touch. Then\n  `game.input.consumeAll()`, a flurry back to the title, and the idle timer resets. The input that exits never\n  activates a menu item.\n- **Determinism:** seeded. Headless, it runs the full loop with no errors (§14).\n\n### 7.24 Multiplayer: AI Hub session and Echo Run (`87-hub.js`, `88-echorun.js`)\n\n**Echo Run** is the Black Run (01C) as a time trial: you play as Dagny from the start gate to the village. Whiteout\nencounters sit at fixed distances with seeded types and warm spots. A Whiteout that reaches you adds **+3 s** and a\nstumble. Each crit takes **0.5 s** off. Three routes: BLUE (safe), BLACK (fast, but with Plows), and THE JUMP (the\nfastest). Ranks: Double Black < 95 s · Black < 110 s · Blue < 130 s · else Green.\n\n**On its own (no hub):** Echo Run from the title. Your best run is recorded (walker edge, s, aim state and persona\nevery 0.1 s, about 1,200 samples) in `localStorage['s7:echo']` and replayed as **YOUR ECHO**: a translucent rig in\npale blue with a name tag. Results show your best time and rank. The campaign itself is single-player. In an AI Hub\nsession the same mode runs over the network (below).\n\n**In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`):\n1. At start, skip the title, attract mode and menus. Boot builds the Black Run world, then\n   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4] })`. If it returns `null`, carry on as the normal game.\n2. Seed the course from `AIHub.rng('course')`. Show \"GET READY\" over the start gate, and call `AIHub.ready()` with no\n   key press. We use the hub's own card (no `card: true`).\n3. On `start`, count 3-2-1 against `AIHub.time()`. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n4. **Send** (unreliable, 10 Hz): `{ t: 'g', area: 'blackrun', e: edgeIndex, s: Math.round(s), a: aiming ? 1 : 0,\n   y: Math.round(yaw * 100) }`. When you finish, send reliably: `{ t: 'done', time }`.\n5. **Receive:** draw each other player as an **echo**: a translucent rig (`actor.fade = .45`) with a scarf in their\n   seat colour (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) and a name tag above (from `world.project`; names are\n   drawn as text, never inserted as HTML). Positions ease toward the latest sample. Echoes affect nothing.\n6. **Progress** about once a second: `AIHub.progress({ score: metresDown, label: '62% down · +6 s' })`.\n7. **Finish:** `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time() + penaltyMs), stats: { Crits, Penalties, Thawed },\n   awards: [{ title: 'Clean Line', detail: 'No penalties' }] })`, once. Then wait, watching the echoes.\n8. **`time-up`:** if you haven't finished, `AIHub.result({ score: metresDown })` at once.\n9. **`end`:** stop input (`game.input.clear()`, ignore everything) and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, stop the\n   music), freeze the sim, and show \"ROUND OVER\". The hub shows the results.\n10. **`leave`:** remove that player's echo.\n11. **Session rules:** no Quit, no Dev Mode, no saves, no map (Create stays free for the hub's Create + Options); the\n    pause menu keeps Resume, Settings, Controls and Help; no `alert` or `confirm`, no new windows or links, no network\n    other than the hub; ignore Options while Create is held (§5.9). On a touch-only device, `AIHub.fail` (§6.5).\n\n**Tests:** the harness (§14.5) with players=2 auto; players=4 with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5; the host-leave\nscenario. Also the game outside a session (`AIHub.active` false): the title appears and Echo Run plays solo with your\necho.\n\n### 7.25 Difficulty, ranks, accessibility\n\n| | Bunny Hill | Piste | Off-Piste |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Enemy damage | ×0.5 | ×1 | ×1.5 |\n| Enemy speed | ×0.85 | ×1 | ×1.15 |\n| Reveal time | ×1.5 | ×1 | ×0.7 |\n| Red drops | ×1.3 | ×1 | ×0.8 |\n| Aim assist default | High | Low | Off |\n| Avalanche speed | ×0.85 | ×1 | ×1.1 |\n\n**Target ranks:** Double Black: crit % ≥ 60, no persona frozen, time ≤ par (Target 00 par 12 min, Target 01 par\n40 min). Black: crit % ≥ 40 and at most 1 frozen. Blue: crit % ≥ 20. Otherwise Green.\n\n**Accessibility:** laugh ripples, warm-spot diamonds, every line subtitled (the voices are gibberish anyway), text\nsize, hold or toggle aim, aim assist, the engine's comfort settings (reduce motion, shake, flashes) respected by every\neffect, rumble from the engine's vibration setting, and no colour-only information.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art direction and rendering\n\n### 8.1 The look\n\n- **The engine's native style:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand`, the 3D picture at `'pixels'` (the game's own resolution,\n  chunky; the `picture3d` setting), characters as **cards** (rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's angle), plus the\n  3D module's **Comic cel** filter (the `filter3d` setting's default; per world `bands: 3, ink: 1, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.4,\n  apply: 'all'`). Light falls in a few flat bands, ink traces edges and silhouettes, colours are pushed.\n- **Killer7's feel, made ours:** large flat areas of white snow and black shadow; one accent colour per area; harsh\n  single key lights and long shadows (the sun or moon with shadows outdoors, a spot or strong point light indoors);\n  saturated **red** only for blood-red things (Red, wounds, the logo, the focus bar). White Whiteouts on white snow are\n  made readable by the ink.\n- **Typography:** chunky capitals, big, centred, hard cuts. Every chapter and boss gets a title card.\n- Run `node engine/tools/check.mjs` (with the CDN routed, §14.4) for its notes on contrast and screen fill, and act on\n  them where they apply to a 3D game.\n\n### 8.2 Palettes and lighting per area\n\n| Area | Accent | Key light | Fill and fog | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Room 7 | candle amber | one hanging lamp (warm), the window's moonlight (cold) | `#1a1418`, fog off | the window always snows |\n| 00A Lobby | oxblood and brass | 3 chandeliers (`#ffd8a0`), moonlight through the revolving door | `#1a1012` | marble checker floor, red runner |\n| 00B Third floor | sick green-white | sconces, one failing (flicker .6) | `#0c100c`, near fog | long corridor sightlines |\n| 00C Shaft | emergency red | a red rotating beacon, the car's own light | `#100406` | vertical space |\n| 01A Village | Glühwein red and candle gold | dusk sun low in the west with shadows; string lights; stall fires (torches) | sky `#2a2440 → #e8a070` | snow ground, timber chalets |\n| 01B Palais | committee blue and grey | cold fluorescent panels (several white lights), flag uplights | `#0a0c14` | marble, glass, flags |\n| 01C Black Run | course orange (piste poles) | floodlights along the piste, the moon | night `#05070f` | orange nets, black signs |\n| 01D Gondola | steel blue and sodium orange | the moon, the cabin's interior light, pylon lamps | storm fog | cable lines against the sky |\n| 01E Archive | glacier cyan | cyan glows from the ice (`world.glow`, light: true) | `#02060a`, close fog | frozen people in the walls |\n| 01F Summit | violet night and Föhn amber | starlight, an amber glow from the pavilion that warms as the boss nears the end | clears from storm to stars | dripping icicles |\n\n### 8.3 Characters (rig specs; `E.Humanoid`, `size: 1.3` unless stated, `look: 'card'`)\n\n| Who | build | outfit, hair, hat | acc | weapon | colours |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ansel | heroic, hunch .15 | coat; short `#9a9aa0`; beanie `#18181c`, pom `#f06a1e` | goggles (amber) on the forehead, pack (red, white stripe) | revolver | skin `#e6c8b0` coat/cloth `#d2461e` pants `#1c1c22` boot `#2a2420` trim `#f4f4f4` |\n| Dagny | heroic | shirt (a speed suit); ponytail `#f0d890`; racehelmet `#c0c8d0`, visor `#ff8a1e` | — | poles | cloth and pants `#1e5cff`, trim `#ffffff`, boot `#101014` |\n| Ignaz | heroic, hunch .1 | coat; short `#e8e8e8`; felt `#2e4a2a`, feather `#e8e0c0` | moustache `#f0f0f0` | rifle | coat `#7a5a3a` pants `#6a4a2a` boot `#8a1a1a` (red socks) trim `#3a2a1a` |\n| Rurik | bulky, size 1.4 | coat (fur); short `#1a1410`; ushanka `#4a3a2a` | beard `#1a1410`, cigar | shotgun (gold) | coat `#3a2a20` trim `#d8b040` pants `#141416` |","numLines":130,"startLine":936,"totalLines":2115}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014XmvqyhSdRGH8Cf6cFVT4a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
