{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PWtS3SNFfMDnYT9DxNv5Du","type":"tool_result","content":"1294\t- **Short, flat sentences**, mostly under 12 words. People answer the question underneath the one asked, or another\n1295\t  one.\n1296\t- **Euphemism as menace:** hotel, bank and ski-school vocabulary for violence (\"check out\", \"turn-down service\",\n1297\t  \"deposit\", \"first tracks\", \"après\").\n1298\t- **Politics as weather, weather as politics:** \"A cold front from the Steppe. A warm one from the Coast. We sell\n1299\t  umbrellas to both.\"\n1300\t- **Repetition with drift:** lines recur and change meaning (\"Breakfast is at seven.\" \"Count again.\").\n1301\t- **Each voice has a tic:**\n1302\t  - Ansel: procedure;\n1303\t  - Dagny: speed;\n1304\t  - Ignaz: hunting and old manners;\n1305\t  - Rurik: prices;\n1306\t  - Kasimir: song;\n1307\t  - Mireille: light and framing;\n1308\t  - Brigid: engineering;\n1309\t  - the Concierge: service;\n1310\t  - Murmel: ellipses and gratuity;\n1311\t  - Pim: counting and 1926;\n1312\t  - Föhn: sunshine;\n1313\t  - Holle: a child's or an oracle's few words.\n1314\t- **Title cards** are in capitals, centred, and hard-cut in with a sting.\n1315\t- **No real nations, politicians, religions or brands.** Swearing is rare and mild. The gore is stylised (red slush,\n1316\t  no organs).\n1317\t- Every line in the demo uses this guide; §11.9 has the key scenes in full, and the rest follow them.\n1318\t\n1319\t### 11.3 Cast\n1320\t\n1321\tThe seven personas (§7.8), Oma Holle, Sister Rosalind, the Concierge (his name plate says AMBROSE), Mister Föhn, Pim\n1322\tthe Lift Boy, Murmel, the targets (Bellcaptain **Augustin Grau**; **Hansi Pulver**, the Powder King), **Die Lustigen\n1323\tVier**, and the tableau extras (delegates, villagers, staff).\n1324\t\n1325\t### 11.4 Enemy table → §7.6. Bosses → §11.8.\n1326\t\n1327\t### 11.5 Items → §7.12.\n1328\t\n1329\t### 11.6 The flow, with timings\n1330\t\n1331\t| # | Beat | Area | Introduces | Approx. minute |\n1332\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1333\t| 1 | Cold open: cards, the phone, \"Shake the bed.\" | Room 7 | dialog, voices, Room 7 | 0 |\n1334\t| 2 | Lobby: walk, turn, junction, first laugh, aim, scan, crit, Red, heal | 00A | the core loop | 1–4 |\n1335\t| 3 | Murmel's free hint; Pim in the elevator (Pin 1) | 00A | hints, lore | 4 |\n1336\t| 4 | Velvet rope: switch to Rurik (ring tutorial), Buyout; the bar fight; the Service Key; the bar phone | 00A | switching, a gate, a key | 5–7 |\n1337\t| 5 | Third floor: doors open on both sides (quick turn), Twins, a Snowballer cart | 00B | enemy variety | 7–9 |\n1338\t| 6 | The lookout: Ignaz's Long Look rings the service bell 70 m away | 00B | Far Bell | 9 |\n1339\t| 7 | The collapsed floor: Dagny's jump | 00B | Ski Jump (indoors) | 9–10 |\n1340\t| 8 | The ceiling falls (scripted): the Sweep's rescue tutorial; Room 7 \"3-7\": save, Wax Bench | 00B | death, rescue, saves, upgrades | 10–11 |\n1341\t| 9 | **Boss: Bellcaptain Grau** in the service shaft; TARGET 00 ELIMINATED; results | 00C | boss, results | 11–14 |\n1342\t| 10 | Briefing: three more coats, TARGET 01 — APRÈS | Room 7 | all seven | 14–15 |\n1343\t| 11 | The village hub: chalets, Glühwein market, Plow intro, Tobogganers; the church bell (Ignaz) clears the lift roof | 01A | hub, choices | 15–20 |\n1344\t| 12 | Palais: security, the Hall of Mirrors (Kasimir's Echo), the Steppe hall Inspector (Edelweiss 1), the press-room darkroom (Mireille), the safe → Ember Charm | 01B | Echo, Exposure, code lock, Inspector | 20–28 |\n1345\t| 13 | **Mid-boss: Die Lustigen Vier** in the ballroom → Edelweiss 2 | 01B | the rhythm boss | 28–31 |\n1346\t| 14 | The T-bar (Rurik's turnstile, aim on the lift); the top station (Room 7, Murmel); the patrol rope (Ansel); the cornice (Brigid) → the shelter, Edelweiss 3 | 01C | Patrol, Cornice, lifts | 31–37 |\n1347\t| 15 | The jump (Dagny) onto the avalanche slope → **LAWINE!** chase; then the downhill to the village | 01C | the avalanche, skiing | 37–40 |\n1348\t| 16 | The Delegate Gate: three passes; the gondola fight; the power cut; Pim on the roof; Ignaz shoots three insulators | 01D | the moving rail, Far Targets | 40–44 |\n1349\t| 17 | The Glacier Archive: the ice gallery, Echo crystals, the ledger Exposure (the reveal), the Ember Charm on the inner vault and the Room 7 door, Blooms, Brigid's seracs | 01E | Bloom, story reveal | 44–50 |\n1350\t| 18 | **Boss: Hansi Pulver**: the Avalaugh, the slalom, the interview; TARGET 01 ELIMINATED; results | 01F | the finale | 50–56 |\n1351\t| 19 | Epilogue: Föhn and Holle play chess; the Concierge's last call; a teaser card; credits | Room 7 | — | 56–58 |\n1352\t\n1353\tTarget 01's hub is non-linear: 01B and 01C can be done in either order; the gondola needs all three passes.\n1354\t\n1355\t### 11.7 Area walkthroughs\n1356\t\n1357\tSizes are in tiles (1 m). Rail graphs are sketches: build them with the listed nodes, then place cameras for every\n1358\tedge. Wave notation: count × type @ spawn. **Bold** = golden path.\n1359\t\n1360\t#### Room 7 (12 × 10; walls 4 m; dark planks; one tall bay window to the north)\n1361\t```\n1362\t          [window]\n1363\t         /        \\\n1364\t     [bed]        [clock]\n1365\t       |             |\n1366\t   [wardrobe]     [bench]\n1367\t         \\        /\n1368\t          [door]  ← every Room 7 door leads here\n1369\t```\n1370\tA two-way loop. Fixed shots: one wide from the south-east corner at 3 m; one low over the bed toward the window; a\n1371\tclose shot of Holle's face for her lines. The props are as in §7.16.\n1372\t\n1373\t#### Target 00 — 00A Grand Hotel Nada, the Lobby (40 × 28; walls 6 m; marble checker floor; red runner)\n1374\t```\n1375\t                          [x1 stairwell door → 00B]  (needs the Service Key)\n1376\t                                    |\n1377\t                              [m1 mezzanine]\n1378\t                                    |  (stairs, 4 m up)\n1379\t [b2 bar back]—[b1 bar]—[g1 velvet rope]—[j3 stairs foot]\n1380\t                          (Rurik, 20 Red)    |\n1381\t                                       [j2 lobby centre]—[j4 elevators: Pim, Pin 1]\n1382\t                                             |\n1383\t              [s1 luggage rack: Murmel]—[j1 reception]—[r7 Room 7 door]\n1384\t                                             |\n1385\t                                  [d0 revolving door]  (storm: locked)\n1386\t```\n1387\tb2 holds the Service Key; b1 holds the bar phone and a Rime crystal (in the fireplace).\n1388\t- **Start:** Room 7 → the r7 door. Tips: walk (r7 → j1), the first junction at j1.\n1389\t- **First Whiteout** (a beat on j1 → j2): a laugh, Ignaz's line, the \"HOLD L2 TO AIM\" tip, a scan tip, one Giggler\n1390\t  (warm spot on its chest) walking out of the dark of the elevators, a fire tip, a crit → \"THAW.\"; the Red tip, a heal\n1391\t  tip once below 70%.\n1392\t- **j4:** Pim in the open elevator car (lore 1, Pin 1 on the car's floor). Wave `elev`: 3 × Giggler @ the shafts.\n1393\t- **s1:** Murmel's free hint 1.\n1394\t- **g1:** the velvet rope. The ring tip (\"HOLD L1: THE FEATHERBED\"), switch to Rurik, pay 20 Red.\n1395\t- **b1:** wave `bar`: 2 × Giggler + 1 × Bellboy from behind the counter. The bar phone (the Concierge, call 2). A Rime\n1396\t  crystal in the fireplace. **b2:** the Service Key behind the bar (a pickup).\n1397\t- **m1:** wave `mezz`: 2 × Bellboy running down from the third floor. x1 needs the Service Key.\n1398\t- Cameras: a high wide shot from the mezzanine looking down over j2; a low dolly along the reception desk; a\n1399\t  through-the-chandelier crane on the stairs; a reverse shot in the bar.\n1400\t- Pickups: Red snow ×2 (tracked in from the storm), a Dossier page (\"Grau's employee file\") at reception.\n1401\t\n1402\t#### 00B Third Floor and the Service Shaft (56 × 20, plus the 8 × 8 shaft at the east end; walls 3 m)\n1403\t```\n1404\t[x1 stair door]—[c1]—[j5: 305 | 306 | on]—[c2]—[l1 LOOKOUT: the service bell 70 m east across the light well]\n1405\t                       |      |                   |\n1406\t                    [r305]  [r306 Twins]          [g2 ceiling hole: JUMP (Dagny)]\n1407\t                                                  |\n1408\t                     [c3: SCRIPTED COLLAPSE]—[j6: Room 7 \"3-7\" | r312 | on]—[c4]—[sh shaft doors (open after the bell)]\n1409\t                                                                                    |\n1410\t                                                                         [00C ring rail round the shaft floor]\n1411\t```\n1412\t- **c1 → c2:** doors open on both sides as you pass (waves `doors1`, `doors2`: 2–3 × Giggler each, from behind you\n1413\t  too: the quick-turn tip). r306: wave `twins` (1 × Twins) and a Rime crystal. r305: a Dossier page (\"Room service\n1414\t  menu: the Bellcaptain's specials\") and Red.\n1415\t- **c2:** a room-service cart with a Snowballer throwing ice cubes from 30 m.\n1416\t- **l1 LOOKOUT:** across the hotel's light well, the giant service bell hangs 70 m away. Only Ignaz's scope reaches it\n1417\t  (Murmel's hint 3 explains if asked). Ringing it: a deep DING, and the shaft doors at the far end grind open\n1418\t  (cutscene: 3 s).\n1419\t- **g2:** the floor has fallen through; Dagny's jump (hint 4).\n1420\t- **c3, scripted:** the ceiling gives way on the active persona → frozen. The Sweep tutorial: Ansel steps out of the\n1421\t  \"3-7\" Room 7 door at j6 and walks back; 2 × Giggler converge on the statue; hold △. Then Rosalind on the radio:\n1422\t  \"The Sweep only leaves Room 7 when someone's on the floor. Use the wardrobe if you want him back.\"\n1423\t- **j6:** Room 7 \"3-7\": save, the Wax Bench tip (Ignaz's first upgrade is suggested). Pin 2 is on the room-service cart\n1424\t  at c2. **sh:** autosave, then Grau.\n1425\t- Pim's appearance 2: sitting on a floating room-service cart at c4.\n1426\t\n1427\t#### 00C Boss — Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (§11.8)\n1428\t\n1429\t#### Target 01 — 01A Oberglück, the Village (64 × 48; snow ground; dusk; chalets as shapes, streets as rails)\n1430\t```\n1431\t                          [pg Palais gate → 01B]\n1432\t                                  |\n1433\t [ch church square]—[f1 fountain ring, north]—[mk market alley]—[r7a Room 7 door (bakery alley)]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"534c80fe-08ee-4872-9ff5-d1fa9fada0c9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:17.993Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Short, flat sentences**, mostly under 12 words. People answer the question underneath the one asked, or another\n  one.\n- **Euphemism as menace:** hotel, bank and ski-school vocabulary for violence (\"check out\", \"turn-down service\",\n  \"deposit\", \"first tracks\", \"après\").\n- **Politics as weather, weather as politics:** \"A cold front from the Steppe. A warm one from the Coast. We sell\n  umbrellas to both.\"\n- **Repetition with drift:** lines recur and change meaning (\"Breakfast is at seven.\" \"Count again.\").\n- **Each voice has a tic:**\n  - Ansel: procedure;\n  - Dagny: speed;\n  - Ignaz: hunting and old manners;\n  - Rurik: prices;\n  - Kasimir: song;\n  - Mireille: light and framing;\n  - Brigid: engineering;\n  - the Concierge: service;\n  - Murmel: ellipses and gratuity;\n  - Pim: counting and 1926;\n  - Föhn: sunshine;\n  - Holle: a child's or an oracle's few words.\n- **Title cards** are in capitals, centred, and hard-cut in with a sting.\n- **No real nations, politicians, religions or brands.** Swearing is rare and mild. The gore is stylised (red slush,\n  no organs).\n- Every line in the demo uses this guide; §11.9 has the key scenes in full, and the rest follow them.\n\n### 11.3 Cast\n\nThe seven personas (§7.8), Oma Holle, Sister Rosalind, the Concierge (his name plate says AMBROSE), Mister Föhn, Pim\nthe Lift Boy, Murmel, the targets (Bellcaptain **Augustin Grau**; **Hansi Pulver**, the Powder King), **Die Lustigen\nVier**, and the tableau extras (delegates, villagers, staff).\n\n### 11.4 Enemy table → §7.6. Bosses → §11.8.\n\n### 11.5 Items → §7.12.\n\n### 11.6 The flow, with timings\n\n| # | Beat | Area | Introduces | Approx. minute |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cold open: cards, the phone, \"Shake the bed.\" | Room 7 | dialog, voices, Room 7 | 0 |\n| 2 | Lobby: walk, turn, junction, first laugh, aim, scan, crit, Red, heal | 00A | the core loop | 1–4 |\n| 3 | Murmel's free hint; Pim in the elevator (Pin 1) | 00A | hints, lore | 4 |\n| 4 | Velvet rope: switch to Rurik (ring tutorial), Buyout; the bar fight; the Service Key; the bar phone | 00A | switching, a gate, a key | 5–7 |\n| 5 | Third floor: doors open on both sides (quick turn), Twins, a Snowballer cart | 00B | enemy variety | 7–9 |\n| 6 | The lookout: Ignaz's Long Look rings the service bell 70 m away | 00B | Far Bell | 9 |\n| 7 | The collapsed floor: Dagny's jump | 00B | Ski Jump (indoors) | 9–10 |\n| 8 | The ceiling falls (scripted): the Sweep's rescue tutorial; Room 7 \"3-7\": save, Wax Bench | 00B | death, rescue, saves, upgrades | 10–11 |\n| 9 | **Boss: Bellcaptain Grau** in the service shaft; TARGET 00 ELIMINATED; results | 00C | boss, results | 11–14 |\n| 10 | Briefing: three more coats, TARGET 01 — APRÈS | Room 7 | all seven | 14–15 |\n| 11 | The village hub: chalets, Glühwein market, Plow intro, Tobogganers; the church bell (Ignaz) clears the lift roof | 01A | hub, choices | 15–20 |\n| 12 | Palais: security, the Hall of Mirrors (Kasimir's Echo), the Steppe hall Inspector (Edelweiss 1), the press-room darkroom (Mireille), the safe → Ember Charm | 01B | Echo, Exposure, code lock, Inspector | 20–28 |\n| 13 | **Mid-boss: Die Lustigen Vier** in the ballroom → Edelweiss 2 | 01B | the rhythm boss | 28–31 |\n| 14 | The T-bar (Rurik's turnstile, aim on the lift); the top station (Room 7, Murmel); the patrol rope (Ansel); the cornice (Brigid) → the shelter, Edelweiss 3 | 01C | Patrol, Cornice, lifts | 31–37 |\n| 15 | The jump (Dagny) onto the avalanche slope → **LAWINE!** chase; then the downhill to the village | 01C | the avalanche, skiing | 37–40 |\n| 16 | The Delegate Gate: three passes; the gondola fight; the power cut; Pim on the roof; Ignaz shoots three insulators | 01D | the moving rail, Far Targets | 40–44 |\n| 17 | The Glacier Archive: the ice gallery, Echo crystals, the ledger Exposure (the reveal), the Ember Charm on the inner vault and the Room 7 door, Blooms, Brigid's seracs | 01E | Bloom, story reveal | 44–50 |\n| 18 | **Boss: Hansi Pulver**: the Avalaugh, the slalom, the interview; TARGET 01 ELIMINATED; results | 01F | the finale | 50–56 |\n| 19 | Epilogue: Föhn and Holle play chess; the Concierge's last call; a teaser card; credits | Room 7 | — | 56–58 |\n\nTarget 01's hub is non-linear: 01B and 01C can be done in either order; the gondola needs all three passes.\n\n### 11.7 Area walkthroughs\n\nSizes are in tiles (1 m). Rail graphs are sketches: build them with the listed nodes, then place cameras for every\nedge. Wave notation: count × type @ spawn. **Bold** = golden path.\n\n#### Room 7 (12 × 10; walls 4 m; dark planks; one tall bay window to the north)\n```\n          [window]\n         /        \\\n     [bed]        [clock]\n       |             |\n   [wardrobe]     [bench]\n         \\        /\n          [door]  ← every Room 7 door leads here\n```\nA two-way loop. Fixed shots: one wide from the south-east corner at 3 m; one low over the bed toward the window; a\nclose shot of Holle's face for her lines. The props are as in §7.16.\n\n#### Target 00 — 00A Grand Hotel Nada, the Lobby (40 × 28; walls 6 m; marble checker floor; red runner)\n```\n                          [x1 stairwell door → 00B]  (needs the Service Key)\n                                    |\n                              [m1 mezzanine]\n                                    |  (stairs, 4 m up)\n [b2 bar back]—[b1 bar]—[g1 velvet rope]—[j3 stairs foot]\n                          (Rurik, 20 Red)    |\n                                       [j2 lobby centre]—[j4 elevators: Pim, Pin 1]\n                                             |\n              [s1 luggage rack: Murmel]—[j1 reception]—[r7 Room 7 door]\n                                             |\n                                  [d0 revolving door]  (storm: locked)\n```\nb2 holds the Service Key; b1 holds the bar phone and a Rime crystal (in the fireplace).\n- **Start:** Room 7 → the r7 door. Tips: walk (r7 → j1), the first junction at j1.\n- **First Whiteout** (a beat on j1 → j2): a laugh, Ignaz's line, the \"HOLD L2 TO AIM\" tip, a scan tip, one Giggler\n  (warm spot on its chest) walking out of the dark of the elevators, a fire tip, a crit → \"THAW.\"; the Red tip, a heal\n  tip once below 70%.\n- **j4:** Pim in the open elevator car (lore 1, Pin 1 on the car's floor). Wave `elev`: 3 × Giggler @ the shafts.\n- **s1:** Murmel's free hint 1.\n- **g1:** the velvet rope. The ring tip (\"HOLD L1: THE FEATHERBED\"), switch to Rurik, pay 20 Red.\n- **b1:** wave `bar`: 2 × Giggler + 1 × Bellboy from behind the counter. The bar phone (the Concierge, call 2). A Rime\n  crystal in the fireplace. **b2:** the Service Key behind the bar (a pickup).\n- **m1:** wave `mezz`: 2 × Bellboy running down from the third floor. x1 needs the Service Key.\n- Cameras: a high wide shot from the mezzanine looking down over j2; a low dolly along the reception desk; a\n  through-the-chandelier crane on the stairs; a reverse shot in the bar.\n- Pickups: Red snow ×2 (tracked in from the storm), a Dossier page (\"Grau's employee file\") at reception.\n\n#### 00B Third Floor and the Service Shaft (56 × 20, plus the 8 × 8 shaft at the east end; walls 3 m)\n```\n[x1 stair door]—[c1]—[j5: 305 | 306 | on]—[c2]—[l1 LOOKOUT: the service bell 70 m east across the light well]\n                       |      |                   |\n                    [r305]  [r306 Twins]          [g2 ceiling hole: JUMP (Dagny)]\n                                                  |\n                     [c3: SCRIPTED COLLAPSE]—[j6: Room 7 \"3-7\" | r312 | on]—[c4]—[sh shaft doors (open after the bell)]\n                                                                                    |\n                                                                         [00C ring rail round the shaft floor]\n```\n- **c1 → c2:** doors open on both sides as you pass (waves `doors1`, `doors2`: 2–3 × Giggler each, from behind you\n  too: the quick-turn tip). r306: wave `twins` (1 × Twins) and a Rime crystal. r305: a Dossier page (\"Room service\n  menu: the Bellcaptain's specials\") and Red.\n- **c2:** a room-service cart with a Snowballer throwing ice cubes from 30 m.\n- **l1 LOOKOUT:** across the hotel's light well, the giant service bell hangs 70 m away. Only Ignaz's scope reaches it\n  (Murmel's hint 3 explains if asked). Ringing it: a deep DING, and the shaft doors at the far end grind open\n  (cutscene: 3 s).\n- **g2:** the floor has fallen through; Dagny's jump (hint 4).\n- **c3, scripted:** the ceiling gives way on the active persona → frozen. The Sweep tutorial: Ansel steps out of the\n  \"3-7\" Room 7 door at j6 and walks back; 2 × Giggler converge on the statue; hold △. Then Rosalind on the radio:\n  \"The Sweep only leaves Room 7 when someone's on the floor. Use the wardrobe if you want him back.\"\n- **j6:** Room 7 \"3-7\": save, the Wax Bench tip (Ignaz's first upgrade is suggested). Pin 2 is on the room-service cart\n  at c2. **sh:** autosave, then Grau.\n- Pim's appearance 2: sitting on a floating room-service cart at c4.\n\n#### 00C Boss — Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (§11.8)\n\n#### Target 01 — 01A Oberglück, the Village (64 × 48; snow ground; dusk; chalets as shapes, streets as rails)\n```\n                          [pg Palais gate → 01B]\n                                  |\n [ch church square]—[f1 fountain ring, north]—[mk market alley]—[r7a Room 7 door (bakery alley)]","numLines":140,"startLine":1294,"totalLines":2116}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PWtS3SNFfMDnYT9DxNv5Du","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
