{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AiNWhVYg8pJX2zf59J8S9S","type":"tool_result","content":"1433\t [ch church square]—[f1 fountain ring, north]—[mk market alley]—[r7a Room 7 door (bakery alley)]\n1434\t   bell tower                     |                  |\n1435\t   (Far Bell from mk, 80 m)  [f2 fountain ring, south]  [mu ski school: Murmel]\n1436\t                                  |\n1437\t       [ht Hotel steps (Target 01 start)]—[ls lift-station square]—[tb turnstile (Rurik, 40) → T-bar → 01C]\n1438\t                                  |\n1439\t                          [gg Delegate Gate (3 Edelweiss) → 01D]\n1440\t```\n1441\t- **Start** at ht after the briefing. The \"THREE MORE COATS ARE DRY\" card; a tip that the ring now has seven.\n1442\t- **ls:** the lift-station hut is buried under a roof drift. Murmel's hint 5: the church bell.\n1443\t- **mk:** the market (Glühwein stalls with real fires, string lights); wave `market`: 3 × Giggler + **1 × Plow** (its\n1444\t  intro; a Rurik or Kasimir tip appears if the Plow takes 4 frontal hits) + 1 × Snowballer on a chalet roof. At the\n1445\t  alley's end, the **lookout** toward the church tower (80 m): Ignaz rings the bell → the drift slides off the lift\n1446\t  station.\n1447\t- **ch:** wave `church`: 2 × Twins. Frozen villagers (tableau lines). Pin 3 on the fountain's frozen basin (f1).\n1448\t- **tb:** the turnstile (Rurik, 40 Red) → the T-bar ride to 01C (aim allowed: 3 × Snowballer on the slope as you rise).\n1449\t- **gg:** the Delegate Gate (three slots). A phone booth by the gate (the Concierge, call 4: Edelweiss).\n1450\t- Pim's appearance 3: above the fountain on his floating seat.\n1451\t- **Returning from 01C** you arrive at **ls** from the slope's bottom (the downhill).\n1452\t\n1453\t#### 01B Palais des Neiges (60 × 40; marble; glass; two delegation halls)\n1454\t```\n1455\t[e1 entrance]—[sc security arch]—[at atrium]—[hm Hall of Mirrors]—(Echo Wall)—[sp servants' passage]—[bb ballroom backstage]\n1456\t                                      |   \\                                                        |\n1457\t                                 [cf Coastal hall]  [sd Steppe hall: INSPECTOR → Edelweiss 1]   [br BALLROOM: the Jolly Four]\n1458\t                                      |   (safe 7-1-2-6 → Ember Charm)       |                         |\n1459\t                                 [pr press room: DARKROOM → the code]  [ck cloakroom: Room 7 door]  [bx back exit → 01A f1]\n1460\t```\n1461\t- **sc:** the metal-detector arch (a scan reminder tip); wave `security`: 2 × Bellboy + 2 × Giggler.\n1462\t- **at:** a phone (the Concierge, call 5: Article Nine).\n1463\t- **cf / sd:** the frozen delegations (tableau lines); waves `coast` (Plow + 2 × Giggler) and `steppe` (2 × Twins).\n1464\t  The **Inspector** blinks between the Steppe hall's three flag stands; kill it for Edelweiss 1.\n1465\t- **pr, darkroom:** the lights are out; Whiteouts here (`dark`: 3 × Giggler) can only be seen by scan or flash. The\n1466\t  blackboard is an Exposure: Mireille's Flash develops \"7-1-2-6\" written in invisible ink under a cartoon of a mountain\n1467\t  (\"26.1.1926\" read backwards) → the Exposure in the Dossier.\n1468\t- **cf safe:** a code lock: 7-1-2-6 → the Ember Charm, plus a Dossier page (\"The Thaw Accord, Article Nine\").\n1469\t- **hm:** the Hall of Mirrors: the Echo Wall (Kasimir) opens the servants' passage. Pin 4 is in the passage. Murmel's\n1470\t  hint 7 covers it.\n1471\t- **br:** autosave, then **the Jolly Four** (§11.8) → Edelweiss 2 (it drops from the tuba's bell) and 10 Rime. The back\n1472\t  exit bx opens to the village (a shortcut).\n1473\t- **ck:** the Room 7 door (behind the coats).\n1474\t\n1475\t#### 01C The Black Run (terrain; top 2,300 m → village 1,700 m; about 1.6 km of piste; night floodlights)\n1476\t```\n1477\t[tb T-bar top]—[ts top station: Room 7 door, Murmel]—[pr PATROL ROPE (Ansel)]—[cr ridge: CORNICE (Brigid)]—[sb snow bridge*]—[as shelter: Edelweiss 3, Pin 5]\n1478\t      |                                                                                                            |\n1479\t [st start gate]                                                                                           [jp JUMP (Dagny)]\n1480\t      ║ ski                                                                                                        ║\n1481\t [f1 fork: BLUE | BLACK | JUMP (Dagny)]                                                                            ║\n1482\t      ║ BLUE: long, gentle, 2 waves                                                                                ║\n1483\t      ║ BLACK: steep, a Plow on the piste, Tobogganers  ◄══ jp lands here (the LAWINE chase, once) ═════════════════╝\n1484\t      ║ JUMP: a kicker over a gully that rejoins BLACK lower down (about 9 s faster)\n1485\t [f2 merge]══ski══[vb village bottom → 01A ls]\n1486\t```\n1487\t(* the snow bridge edge exists only after the cornice falls.)\n1488\t- **ts:** a Room 7 door (so the Sweep can be fetched for the patrol rope), Murmel's hints 9 and 10, Red snow.\n1489\t- **pr:** the patrol rope (\"CLOSED — AVALANCHE DANGER — PATROL ONLY\"): only Ansel crosses.\n1490\t- **cr:** the ridge wears a cornice over a crevasse. Switch to Brigid; a Control Charge brings it down → a snow\n1491\t  bridge edge (sb) appears (cutscene: 4 s).\n1492\t- **as:** the avalanche shelter: Edelweiss 3, Pin 5, the Dossier page \"The Avalanche of 1926\" (a clipping with a team\n1493\t  photo of eight). Wave `shelter` (2 × Giggler) on the way out.\n1494\t- **jp:** the way back down is a ski jump (Dagny). Landing on the black slope starts **LAWINE!** (once):\n1495\t  - the camera cuts to a reverse tracking shot (looking back up at Dagny with the wall of white behind);\n1496\t  - 25 s of downhill; the avalanche runs at 92% of Dagny's tucked top speed;\n1497\t  - letting go of tuck for more than 1.5 s lets it catch up, and if it reaches her she freezes (the Sweep spawns at\n1498\t    the top station);\n1499\t  - Whiteout faces laugh in the snow wall;\n1500\t  - 2 forks to choose under pressure.\n1501\t- **st → f1 → f2 → vb:** the normal downhill. BLUE: waves `blue1` (3 × Giggler on skis: Tobogganer movement, Giggler\n1502\t  stats) and `blue2` (2 × Tobogganer). BLACK: `black1` (a Plow standing on the piste: hockey-stop and deal with it, or\n1503\t  take the jump), `black2` (3 × Tobogganer). JUMP (Dagny): a kicker over a gully, a slow-motion beat in the air (time\n1504\t  ×0.5 for 0.6 s, a fixed side-on shot), then it rejoins BLACK below `black1`. Floodlit fixed shots at the steep bits;\n1505\t  follow shots otherwise.\n1506\t- **The T-bar up (from 01A):** a lift edge of about 30 s with Snowballers on the slope (aim on the lift).\n1507\t- Echo Run uses st → vb with its own wave table (§11.11).\n1508\t\n1509\t#### 01D Himmelsbahn, the Gondola (terrain valley; a lift edge of about 1.8 km over about 120 s; storm)\n1510\t```\n1511\t[gs village station]==lift 0→55%==[mid: POWER CUT]==lift 55→100%==[gl glacier station → 01E]\n1512\t```\n1513\t- Board at gs after the Delegate Gate ceremony (the three passes glow into their slots; 3 chimes). The cabin is a pen\n1514\t  and shape model; the camera is inside (fixed shots through the windows) until you aim.\n1515\t- **Combat while riding:**\n1516\t  - cabins on the down cable pass every 15 s with a Snowballer leaning out;\n1517\t  - **Cable Crawlers** (Gigglers, hand over hand along our cable toward the cabin; they explode on the roof: 20 damage\n1518\t    and a lurch);\n1519\t  - 2 × Giggler appear at the windows (they climb up from below).\n1520\t- **mid:** the power cuts; the cabin swings; Pim sits on the roof (lore 4: \"Count again.\"); Oma Holle's voice in a\n1521\t  dream fragment. Three frozen **insulators** on the next pylon, 70–90 m away: only Ignaz's scope (Far Targets).\n1522\t  Then the power comes back and the ride continues. Pin 6 is wedged in the cabin's seat.\n1523\t- **gl:** autosave; the glacier tunnel.\n1524\t\n1525\t#### 01E The Glacier Archive (50 × 40; blue ice walls; dark; cyan glows)\n1526\t```\n1527\t[gl tunnel]—[ig ice gallery: frozen people]—[ec ECHO CRYSTALS (Kasimir)]—[lv ledger vault: EXPOSURE (Mireille)]\n1528\t                     |                                                       |\n1529\t              [r7e Room 7 door: ICE LOCK (Ember Charm)]            [iv inner vault: ICE LOCK (Ember Charm)]\n1530\t                                                                             |\n1531\t                                                                [sr SERACS (Brigid)]—[fe freight elevator → 01F]\n1532\t```\n1533\t- **ig:** the ice gallery: deposit boxes and people frozen in the walls (tableau lines with account numbers). Pim's\n1534\t  appearance 5. Wave `gallery`: 3 × Giggler + 1 × Twins. Pin 7 is behind an ice-crystal side branch (Echo).\n1535\t- **ec:** resonant crystals block the corridor; Kasimir's Echo shatters them (hint 11 if needed).\n1536\t- **r7e:** the Room 7 door is frozen in the wall: use the Ember Charm.\n1537\t- **lv:** the frozen ledger on a lectern: Mireille's Flash develops it. The reveal: \"ACCOUNT 7 — HOLDER: H. HOLLE —\n1538\t  CONTENTS: SEVEN (7) PERSONS, DECEASED 26.1.1926 — IN TRUST.\" Then the persona chatter (§11.9).\n1539\t- **iv:** the inner vault (the Ember Charm): 15 Rime, a Dossier page (\"The Department of Discretion: Standing Orders\").\n1540\t  First **Bloom** (wave `vault`: 1 × Bloom + 2 × Giggler).\n1541\t- **sr:** the seracs block the freight elevator: Brigid's Control Charge. **fe:** autosave, then the summit.\n1542\t\n1543\t#### 01F The Summit (terrain; the summit plaza with the glass pavilion; the glacier face below; the old chairlift)\n1544\tPhase rails: the plaza's **arc rail** (a 120° arc of 30 m radius round the pavilion, 5 nodes behind cover: two\n1545\tflagpoles, the weather mast, two pavilion pillars); the **slalom rail** (about 700 m down the glacier face, parallel\n1546\tto Hansi's own rail 15–25 m to the side); the **chairlift** (a fixed first-person scene). See §11.8.\n1547\t\n1548\t#### Epilogue (Room 7) → §11.9.\n1549\t\n1550\t### 11.8 Bosses\n1551\t\n1552\t**Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (00C, the service shaft; 2–3 min; no switching after the intro).**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"46ea9692-de21-429a-99c8-5b7e448c9f31","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:29.166Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":" [ch church square]—[f1 fountain ring, north]—[mk market alley]—[r7a Room 7 door (bakery alley)]\n   bell tower                     |                  |\n   (Far Bell from mk, 80 m)  [f2 fountain ring, south]  [mu ski school: Murmel]\n                                  |\n       [ht Hotel steps (Target 01 start)]—[ls lift-station square]—[tb turnstile (Rurik, 40) → T-bar → 01C]\n                                  |\n                          [gg Delegate Gate (3 Edelweiss) → 01D]\n```\n- **Start** at ht after the briefing. The \"THREE MORE COATS ARE DRY\" card; a tip that the ring now has seven.\n- **ls:** the lift-station hut is buried under a roof drift. Murmel's hint 5: the church bell.\n- **mk:** the market (Glühwein stalls with real fires, string lights); wave `market`: 3 × Giggler + **1 × Plow** (its\n  intro; a Rurik or Kasimir tip appears if the Plow takes 4 frontal hits) + 1 × Snowballer on a chalet roof. At the\n  alley's end, the **lookout** toward the church tower (80 m): Ignaz rings the bell → the drift slides off the lift\n  station.\n- **ch:** wave `church`: 2 × Twins. Frozen villagers (tableau lines). Pin 3 on the fountain's frozen basin (f1).\n- **tb:** the turnstile (Rurik, 40 Red) → the T-bar ride to 01C (aim allowed: 3 × Snowballer on the slope as you rise).\n- **gg:** the Delegate Gate (three slots). A phone booth by the gate (the Concierge, call 4: Edelweiss).\n- Pim's appearance 3: above the fountain on his floating seat.\n- **Returning from 01C** you arrive at **ls** from the slope's bottom (the downhill).\n\n#### 01B Palais des Neiges (60 × 40; marble; glass; two delegation halls)\n```\n[e1 entrance]—[sc security arch]—[at atrium]—[hm Hall of Mirrors]—(Echo Wall)—[sp servants' passage]—[bb ballroom backstage]\n                                      |   \\                                                        |\n                                 [cf Coastal hall]  [sd Steppe hall: INSPECTOR → Edelweiss 1]   [br BALLROOM: the Jolly Four]\n                                      |   (safe 7-1-2-6 → Ember Charm)       |                         |\n                                 [pr press room: DARKROOM → the code]  [ck cloakroom: Room 7 door]  [bx back exit → 01A f1]\n```\n- **sc:** the metal-detector arch (a scan reminder tip); wave `security`: 2 × Bellboy + 2 × Giggler.\n- **at:** a phone (the Concierge, call 5: Article Nine).\n- **cf / sd:** the frozen delegations (tableau lines); waves `coast` (Plow + 2 × Giggler) and `steppe` (2 × Twins).\n  The **Inspector** blinks between the Steppe hall's three flag stands; kill it for Edelweiss 1.\n- **pr, darkroom:** the lights are out; Whiteouts here (`dark`: 3 × Giggler) can only be seen by scan or flash. The\n  blackboard is an Exposure: Mireille's Flash develops \"7-1-2-6\" written in invisible ink under a cartoon of a mountain\n  (\"26.1.1926\" read backwards) → the Exposure in the Dossier.\n- **cf safe:** a code lock: 7-1-2-6 → the Ember Charm, plus a Dossier page (\"The Thaw Accord, Article Nine\").\n- **hm:** the Hall of Mirrors: the Echo Wall (Kasimir) opens the servants' passage. Pin 4 is in the passage. Murmel's\n  hint 7 covers it.\n- **br:** autosave, then **the Jolly Four** (§11.8) → Edelweiss 2 (it drops from the tuba's bell) and 10 Rime. The back\n  exit bx opens to the village (a shortcut).\n- **ck:** the Room 7 door (behind the coats).\n\n#### 01C The Black Run (terrain; top 2,300 m → village 1,700 m; about 1.6 km of piste; night floodlights)\n```\n[tb T-bar top]—[ts top station: Room 7 door, Murmel]—[pr PATROL ROPE (Ansel)]—[cr ridge: CORNICE (Brigid)]—[sb snow bridge*]—[as shelter: Edelweiss 3, Pin 5]\n      |                                                                                                            |\n [st start gate]                                                                                           [jp JUMP (Dagny)]\n      ║ ski                                                                                                        ║\n [f1 fork: BLUE | BLACK | JUMP (Dagny)]                                                                            ║\n      ║ BLUE: long, gentle, 2 waves                                                                                ║\n      ║ BLACK: steep, a Plow on the piste, Tobogganers  ◄══ jp lands here (the LAWINE chase, once) ═════════════════╝\n      ║ JUMP: a kicker over a gully that rejoins BLACK lower down (about 9 s faster)\n [f2 merge]══ski══[vb village bottom → 01A ls]\n```\n(* the snow bridge edge exists only after the cornice falls.)\n- **ts:** a Room 7 door (so the Sweep can be fetched for the patrol rope), Murmel's hints 9 and 10, Red snow.\n- **pr:** the patrol rope (\"CLOSED — AVALANCHE DANGER — PATROL ONLY\"): only Ansel crosses.\n- **cr:** the ridge wears a cornice over a crevasse. Switch to Brigid; a Control Charge brings it down → a snow\n  bridge edge (sb) appears (cutscene: 4 s).\n- **as:** the avalanche shelter: Edelweiss 3, Pin 5, the Dossier page \"The Avalanche of 1926\" (a clipping with a team\n  photo of eight). Wave `shelter` (2 × Giggler) on the way out.\n- **jp:** the way back down is a ski jump (Dagny). Landing on the black slope starts **LAWINE!** (once):\n  - the camera cuts to a reverse tracking shot (looking back up at Dagny with the wall of white behind);\n  - 25 s of downhill; the avalanche runs at 92% of Dagny's tucked top speed;\n  - letting go of tuck for more than 1.5 s lets it catch up, and if it reaches her she freezes (the Sweep spawns at\n    the top station);\n  - Whiteout faces laugh in the snow wall;\n  - 2 forks to choose under pressure.\n- **st → f1 → f2 → vb:** the normal downhill. BLUE: waves `blue1` (3 × Giggler on skis: Tobogganer movement, Giggler\n  stats) and `blue2` (2 × Tobogganer). BLACK: `black1` (a Plow standing on the piste: hockey-stop and deal with it, or\n  take the jump), `black2` (3 × Tobogganer). JUMP (Dagny): a kicker over a gully, a slow-motion beat in the air (time\n  ×0.5 for 0.6 s, a fixed side-on shot), then it rejoins BLACK below `black1`. Floodlit fixed shots at the steep bits;\n  follow shots otherwise.\n- **The T-bar up (from 01A):** a lift edge of about 30 s with Snowballers on the slope (aim on the lift).\n- Echo Run uses st → vb with its own wave table (§11.11).\n\n#### 01D Himmelsbahn, the Gondola (terrain valley; a lift edge of about 1.8 km over about 120 s; storm)\n```\n[gs village station]==lift 0→55%==[mid: POWER CUT]==lift 55→100%==[gl glacier station → 01E]\n```\n- Board at gs after the Delegate Gate ceremony (the three passes glow into their slots; 3 chimes). The cabin is a pen\n  and shape model; the camera is inside (fixed shots through the windows) until you aim.\n- **Combat while riding:**\n  - cabins on the down cable pass every 15 s with a Snowballer leaning out;\n  - **Cable Crawlers** (Gigglers, hand over hand along our cable toward the cabin; they explode on the roof: 20 damage\n    and a lurch);\n  - 2 × Giggler appear at the windows (they climb up from below).\n- **mid:** the power cuts; the cabin swings; Pim sits on the roof (lore 4: \"Count again.\"); Oma Holle's voice in a\n  dream fragment. Three frozen **insulators** on the next pylon, 70–90 m away: only Ignaz's scope (Far Targets).\n  Then the power comes back and the ride continues. Pin 6 is wedged in the cabin's seat.\n- **gl:** autosave; the glacier tunnel.\n\n#### 01E The Glacier Archive (50 × 40; blue ice walls; dark; cyan glows)\n```\n[gl tunnel]—[ig ice gallery: frozen people]—[ec ECHO CRYSTALS (Kasimir)]—[lv ledger vault: EXPOSURE (Mireille)]\n                     |                                                       |\n              [r7e Room 7 door: ICE LOCK (Ember Charm)]            [iv inner vault: ICE LOCK (Ember Charm)]\n                                                                             |\n                                                                [sr SERACS (Brigid)]—[fe freight elevator → 01F]\n```\n- **ig:** the ice gallery: deposit boxes and people frozen in the walls (tableau lines with account numbers). Pim's\n  appearance 5. Wave `gallery`: 3 × Giggler + 1 × Twins. Pin 7 is behind an ice-crystal side branch (Echo).\n- **ec:** resonant crystals block the corridor; Kasimir's Echo shatters them (hint 11 if needed).\n- **r7e:** the Room 7 door is frozen in the wall: use the Ember Charm.\n- **lv:** the frozen ledger on a lectern: Mireille's Flash develops it. The reveal: \"ACCOUNT 7 — HOLDER: H. HOLLE —\n  CONTENTS: SEVEN (7) PERSONS, DECEASED 26.1.1926 — IN TRUST.\" Then the persona chatter (§11.9).\n- **iv:** the inner vault (the Ember Charm): 15 Rime, a Dossier page (\"The Department of Discretion: Standing Orders\").\n  First **Bloom** (wave `vault`: 1 × Bloom + 2 × Giggler).\n- **sr:** the seracs block the freight elevator: Brigid's Control Charge. **fe:** autosave, then the summit.\n\n#### 01F The Summit (terrain; the summit plaza with the glass pavilion; the glacier face below; the old chairlift)\nPhase rails: the plaza's **arc rail** (a 120° arc of 30 m radius round the pavilion, 5 nodes behind cover: two\nflagpoles, the weather mast, two pavilion pillars); the **slalom rail** (about 700 m down the glacier face, parallel\nto Hansi's own rail 15–25 m to the side); the **chairlift** (a fixed first-person scene). See §11.8.\n\n#### Epilogue (Room 7) → §11.9.\n\n### 11.8 Bosses\n\n**Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (00C, the service shaft; 2–3 min; no switching after the intro).**","numLines":120,"startLine":1433,"totalLines":2116}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AiNWhVYg8pJX2zf59J8S9S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
