{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2m9UKnR26HTiMgJeFw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012E7Fz25JkftGabGt3UyPrs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":1550,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":538579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":620},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"e9572c43-2c1e-44af-90ea-c39d2c1c98d6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:48.283Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2m9DwXfVm5fMuRaz32","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012E7Fz25JkftGabGt3UyPrs":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","offset":1550,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012E7Fz25JkftGabGt3UyPrs","type":"tool_result","content":"1550\t### 11.8 Bosses\n1551\t\n1552\t**Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (00C, the service shaft; 2–3 min; no switching after the intro).**\n1553\t- **Arena:** the shaft floor (8 × 8) with a ring rail of 4 nodes (walk to dodge); the elevator car runs up and down\n1554\t  the shaft; its doors face your side when it stops at floors 1, 2 and 3 (high above you).\n1555\t- **Phase 1:** the car stops at a floor (\"DING\"). Grau throws 3 suitcases in arcs (shoot them in the air for Red; one\n1556\t  that lands deals 12 damage, and one in three releases a Giggler). After throwing he **tips his hat** for 1.4 s:\n1557\t  his warm spot is under it. A crit ends the phase.\n1558\t- **Phase 2:** the cable snaps. The car free-falls and bounces between floors every 7 s with faster dings; suitcases\n1559\t  fly from both sides; same hat-tip windows.\n1560\t- **Phase 3:** he rides the car's roof ringing his bell; 2 Gigglers drop from above every 6 s; the hat-tip window\n1561\t  shrinks to 1 s.\n1562\t- **Defeat:** \"Checkout… is at… eleven…\" He melts into slush; his bell rolls to your feet. TARGET 00 — AUGUSTIN GRAU —\n1563\t  ELIMINATED. Results.\n1564\t\n1565\t**Die Lustigen Vier, the Jolly Four (01B ballroom; 3 min; switching allowed).**\n1566\t- The four stand on the stage; the `band` song plays. **Each musician's warm spot glows only while their own track\n1567\t  has a note sounding** (from `audio.pos.at` and the track's note string; this works headless on the music clock).\n1568\t  Shots outside a musician's window are absorbed (\"the music protects them\": a deflect sparkle).\n1569\t- Each bar while the band lives, 2 dancing Gigglers waltz in from the dance floor (at most 6 alive), laughing on the\n1570\t  beat.\n1571\t- **Killing a musician** (a crit in their window, or 120 body damage inside windows) removes their track from the\n1572\t  song (`audio.layer(name, 0)`) and raises the tempo (`audio.tempo`): 112 → 124 → 136 → 148.\n1573\t- **The last one alive plays a solo** (the tuba, if left for last: the warm spot sits in the tuba's bell).\n1574\t- **Defeat:** \"Bravo… bravo…\" BRAVO splash. Edelweiss 2 drops from the tuba; 10 Rime.\n1575\t\n1576\t**Hansi Pulver, the Powder King (01F; 6–8 min; an autosave before each phase).**\n1577\t- **Intro (the plaza):** \"Grüß Gott! You came for a lesson? Lesson one: everything goes downhill.\" He laughs, the\n1578\t  Föhn blows, and the snow of the plaza rises into the Avalaugh.\n1579\t- **Phase 1, the Avalaugh** (the arc rail; switching allowed):\n1580\t  - a 12 m laughing snowman with **5 warm spots**: three gold medals on its chest and its two coal eyes;\n1581\t  - it hurls snowballs every 2.2 s (15 damage; shootable);\n1582\t  - a Giggler buds from its base every 5 s;\n1583\t  - each crit melts part of it (a ball shrinks and drips);\n1584\t  - with 2 spots left it sinks and starts **the Thaw**: 40 s, shown as a ring of meltwater spreading across the\n1585\t    plaza. If the timer ends, it bursts for 60 damage and regrows one spot;\n1586\t  - after all 5 the snow collapses, and Hansi falls out of it, clicks into his skis and drops down the glacier face.\n1587\t- **Phase 2, the Slalom** (the slalom rail, `aimOnTheMove`; time ×0.6 while aiming; no switching; any persona, though\n1588\t  Dagny's tuck keeps you close):\n1589\t  - he weaves through 6 slalom gates on his own rail;\n1590\t  - **he can only be hurt while passing a gate** (0.8 s; the flags flash red);\n1591\t  - between gates he throws gold medals (10 damage; shootable);\n1592\t  - you need **4 crits** (or 360 body damage within windows);\n1593\t  - if you fall more than 60 m behind he waits at the next gate, laughing (\"Bend the knees!\");\n1594\t  - after the fourth hit he crashes through the last gate into the old chairlift station.\n1595\t- **Phase 3, the Interview:** a cutscene. The two of you sit on a stuck chairlift in fog; he is human again, losing\n1596\t  warmth. You are in first person, aim only (no scan or skill). His lines play (§11.9). A shot at any time ends it.\n1597\t  If you haven't fired after 10 s, he says the \"You hesitate\" line and lets himself fall. Either way: TARGET 01 — HANSI\n1598\t  PULVER — ELIMINATED; results. The two endings differ by one line and one Dossier note (\"Shot\" or \"Fell\").\n1599\t\n1600\t### 11.9 Script: the key scenes in full\n1601\t\n1602\tSpeaker tags map to `people` ids. Cards are in capitals.\n1603\t\n1604\t**Cold open (Room 7).**\n1605\t```\n1606\tCARD  THE WINTER OF THE THAW ACCORD.\n1607\tCARD  THE FREE CANTON OF PIZ NADA. POPULATION: DISCREET.\n1608\t(The phone rings. Rosalind lifts the receiver and holds it out toward the bed.)\n1609\tCONCIERGE  Good evening, Madame Holle. A guest has checked into the Grand Hotel who will not be checking out.\n1610\tCONCIERGE  Bellcaptain Grau. Third floor and below. The Department thanks you for your discretion.\n1611\tHOLLE      ...Shake the bed, Rosalind.\n1612\tROSALIND   She means it's time. She always means it's time.\n1613\t(Rosalind shakes the featherbed. Feathers. Outside, the snow thickens. The wardrobe doors swing open.)\n1614\tIGNAZ      Grau. His grandfather carried my luggage in 1925. He never smiled either.\n1615\tDAGNY      This one's smiling.\n1616\tRURIK      Everyone smiles when the price is right.\n1617\tCARD  TARGET 00 — TURN-DOWN SERVICE\n1618\t```\n1619\t\n1620\t**First Whiteout (00A).**\n1621\t```\n1622\t(A laugh, somewhere in the dark of the elevators.)\n1623\tIGNAZ   Laughter. In a hotel lobby. At this hour.\n1624\tDAGNY   Shoot it before it finishes the joke.\n1625\t(The first crit) IGNAZ   Clean.\n1626\t```\n1627\t\n1628\t**Murmel (first meeting, 00A).**\n1629\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc","uuid":"3c5962a8-41e6-4f36-a9a1-c66e01ee9d5a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:48.289Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 11.8 Bosses\n\n**Bellcaptain Augustin Grau (00C, the service shaft; 2–3 min; no switching after the intro).**\n- **Arena:** the shaft floor (8 × 8) with a ring rail of 4 nodes (walk to dodge); the elevator car runs up and down\n  the shaft; its doors face your side when it stops at floors 1, 2 and 3 (high above you).\n- **Phase 1:** the car stops at a floor (\"DING\"). Grau throws 3 suitcases in arcs (shoot them in the air for Red; one\n  that lands deals 12 damage, and one in three releases a Giggler). After throwing he **tips his hat** for 1.4 s:\n  his warm spot is under it. A crit ends the phase.\n- **Phase 2:** the cable snaps. The car free-falls and bounces between floors every 7 s with faster dings; suitcases\n  fly from both sides; same hat-tip windows.\n- **Phase 3:** he rides the car's roof ringing his bell; 2 Gigglers drop from above every 6 s; the hat-tip window\n  shrinks to 1 s.\n- **Defeat:** \"Checkout… is at… eleven…\" He melts into slush; his bell rolls to your feet. TARGET 00 — AUGUSTIN GRAU —\n  ELIMINATED. Results.\n\n**Die Lustigen Vier, the Jolly Four (01B ballroom; 3 min; switching allowed).**\n- The four stand on the stage; the `band` song plays. **Each musician's warm spot glows only while their own track\n  has a note sounding** (from `audio.pos.at` and the track's note string; this works headless on the music clock).\n  Shots outside a musician's window are absorbed (\"the music protects them\": a deflect sparkle).\n- Each bar while the band lives, 2 dancing Gigglers waltz in from the dance floor (at most 6 alive), laughing on the\n  beat.\n- **Killing a musician** (a crit in their window, or 120 body damage inside windows) removes their track from the\n  song (`audio.layer(name, 0)`) and raises the tempo (`audio.tempo`): 112 → 124 → 136 → 148.\n- **The last one alive plays a solo** (the tuba, if left for last: the warm spot sits in the tuba's bell).\n- **Defeat:** \"Bravo… bravo…\" BRAVO splash. Edelweiss 2 drops from the tuba; 10 Rime.\n\n**Hansi Pulver, the Powder King (01F; 6–8 min; an autosave before each phase).**\n- **Intro (the plaza):** \"Grüß Gott! You came for a lesson? Lesson one: everything goes downhill.\" He laughs, the\n  Föhn blows, and the snow of the plaza rises into the Avalaugh.\n- **Phase 1, the Avalaugh** (the arc rail; switching allowed):\n  - a 12 m laughing snowman with **5 warm spots**: three gold medals on its chest and its two coal eyes;\n  - it hurls snowballs every 2.2 s (15 damage; shootable);\n  - a Giggler buds from its base every 5 s;\n  - each crit melts part of it (a ball shrinks and drips);\n  - with 2 spots left it sinks and starts **the Thaw**: 40 s, shown as a ring of meltwater spreading across the\n    plaza. If the timer ends, it bursts for 60 damage and regrows one spot;\n  - after all 5 the snow collapses, and Hansi falls out of it, clicks into his skis and drops down the glacier face.\n- **Phase 2, the Slalom** (the slalom rail, `aimOnTheMove`; time ×0.6 while aiming; no switching; any persona, though\n  Dagny's tuck keeps you close):\n  - he weaves through 6 slalom gates on his own rail;\n  - **he can only be hurt while passing a gate** (0.8 s; the flags flash red);\n  - between gates he throws gold medals (10 damage; shootable);\n  - you need **4 crits** (or 360 body damage within windows);\n  - if you fall more than 60 m behind he waits at the next gate, laughing (\"Bend the knees!\");\n  - after the fourth hit he crashes through the last gate into the old chairlift station.\n- **Phase 3, the Interview:** a cutscene. The two of you sit on a stuck chairlift in fog; he is human again, losing\n  warmth. You are in first person, aim only (no scan or skill). His lines play (§11.9). A shot at any time ends it.\n  If you haven't fired after 10 s, he says the \"You hesitate\" line and lets himself fall. Either way: TARGET 01 — HANSI\n  PULVER — ELIMINATED; results. The two endings differ by one line and one Dossier note (\"Shot\" or \"Fell\").\n\n### 11.9 Script: the key scenes in full\n\nSpeaker tags map to `people` ids. Cards are in capitals.\n\n**Cold open (Room 7).**\n```\nCARD  THE WINTER OF THE THAW ACCORD.\nCARD  THE FREE CANTON OF PIZ NADA. POPULATION: DISCREET.\n(The phone rings. Rosalind lifts the receiver and holds it out toward the bed.)\nCONCIERGE  Good evening, Madame Holle. A guest has checked into the Grand Hotel who will not be checking out.\nCONCIERGE  Bellcaptain Grau. Third floor and below. The Department thanks you for your discretion.\nHOLLE      ...Shake the bed, Rosalind.\nROSALIND   She means it's time. She always means it's time.\n(Rosalind shakes the featherbed. Feathers. Outside, the snow thickens. The wardrobe doors swing open.)\nIGNAZ      Grau. His grandfather carried my luggage in 1925. He never smiled either.\nDAGNY      This one's smiling.\nRURIK      Everyone smiles when the price is right.\nCARD  TARGET 00 — TURN-DOWN SERVICE\n```\n\n**First Whiteout (00A).**\n```\n(A laugh, somewhere in the dark of the elevators.)\nIGNAZ   Laughter. In a hotel lobby. At this hour.\nDAGNY   Shoot it before it finishes the joke.\n(The first crit) IGNAZ   Clean.\n```\n\n**Murmel (first meeting, 00A).**\n```","numLines":80,"startLine":1550,"totalLines":2116}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012E7Fz25JkftGabGt3UyPrs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
